{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club","id":1550253,"title":"Running the Free States - 7 - San Francisco and the Vampire Club","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-18T18:21:28-07:00","id":1550253,"title":"Running the Free States - 7 - San Francisco and the Vampire Club","content":"Sam Francisco could play a possible important role in an Anarch Free State chronicle. However, it's important to note that canon is not consistent.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548316#post1548316\">In an earlier post</a> referencing San Francisco, I stated:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council?p=1548316#post1548316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">San Francisco never got its own city book despite a lot of things being established about it. A lot of early WoD fiction was set place in San Francisco, so we do get a lot of information if you bother to read these novels and short stories. More importantly we get a write up of &quot;the Vampire Club&quot; in A World of Darkness, 1e. Despite San Francisco being Camarilla, it is intended as a kind of &quot;Casablanca&quot; where all kinds of vampires can meet and intrigue with the Vampire Club being analogous to Rick's Cafe Americain. Very unusually, it mentions that it was the site of the 1946 Conclave that resulted in the \u201cPalatine Treaty\u201d which gave the domain of San Francisco almost unheard of autonomy. The domain of San Francisco was called the Palatinate of San Francisco, and its Primogen the Palatine Council.<br /> <br /> In historical terms, &quot;palatines&quot; were usually lower lords who nevertheless assumed some of the functions that normally the crown itself would have. In this case, presumably the Prince of San Francisco might be invested with powers normally delegated to the Justicars. Whether that is actually the case is unknown.<br /> <br /> It's not clear to me what exactly that may mean, but I am leaning to the idea that the Justicars and Archons leave it alone even though the domain is governed by Camarilla standards. Presumably there are a lot more details in the &quot;Treaty&quot; that would proscribe when the Justicars might intervene. Presumably this is to justify its status as &quot;Casablanca&quot; in its &quot;Vichy, but Neutral&quot; role. Prince Vannevar Thomas himself is probably more of a Major Strasser type with Sebastian Melmoth more like Captain Renault and Tex R Cainan as Rick Blaine.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs do seem to view San Francisco and Prince Vannevar Thomas as a threat, but presumably its nebulous status suits both the Anarchs and Justicar Petrodon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is even referenced in the Anarch Cookbook which states:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anarch Cookbook, page 41</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free States cover the northwestern coast of Mexico, through San Diego and Los Angeles, to the neutral Palatinate of San Francisco.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, this is not the case in the Los Angeles By Night sourcebook. San Francisco is not stated to be any kind of &quot;palatinate&quot; and is just treated as the closest Camarilla bastion that threatens LA.<br /> <br /> This thread is to be talk about the various canonical San Francisco in the World of Darkness, and how it can be used in a chronicle that concentrates on the Anarch Free States.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-02-2026, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T18:41:58-07:00","id":1550254,"title":"","content":"Let's start with some basic information on the domain of San Francisco as it existed in the early nineties. It was mostly detailed in a series of fictional short stories and novels. I think there was an intent to publish a San Francisco By Night sourcevook, but this did not happen in the early editions. Only in the Revised Era after Kindred of the East corebook was published was such a sourcebook printed, and it clearly was not along the lines of what the early game envisioned.<br /> <br /> Although intended as some kind of &quot;neutral ground&quot; between Anarchs and the Camarilla, the domain itself was governed as any other typical city. It had a prince and primogen council.<br /> <br /> Vannevar Thomas was the Ventrue Prince of San Francisco. The primogen consisted of:<ul><li>Tomaine (Brujah)</li> <li>Alicia McGreb (Gangrel)</li> <li>Bloody Mary (Malkavian)</li> <li>The Dowager (Nosferatu)</li> <li>Allanyan Serata (Toreador)</li> <li>Honerius (Tremere)</li> <li>Nickoli (Ventrue)</li> </ul><br /> So domestically, it was the typical Camarilla city. However, it was supposed to feel like a neutral domain inbetween Anarch and Camarilla. How can we achieve this in practice?<br /> <br /> In the movie Casablanca, those who resisted the Nazis and wanted freedom would go to the city, but be trapped there unless they could receive &quot;letters of transit&quot;. The authorities were not hostile to people there, but collaborated with the Nazis. This is not mirrored well in the setting. If people want to get the Free States, they can. They have no reason to go to San Francisco. Instead, it is a bit inverse. Someone from a Camarilla domain who wants to visit an anarch should visit San Francisco instead and not the Free States. Why?<br /> <br /> Because the lack of any kind of law and order in Los Angeles means that visiting Kindred could get killed. It just takes one jackass, and you are dead. Instead, you should visit San Francisco where your safety is guaranteed. Your anarch childe/sire/friend/old ally/etc. from Los Angeles can then meet you in the Vampire Club where their safety too is guaranteed.<br /> <br /> In the LABN sourcebook, Prince Vannevar Thomas is just one more scheming Camarilla Prince who wants to overthrow the Free States. In earlier sourcebooks, he is the Palatine Prince of an independent domain - backed by the Justicars unlike Siegfried's domain in Vancouver - who will guarantee the safety of Los Angeles Anarchs who visit there (assuming at least they do not create trouble in the Bay Area).<br /> <br /> Obviously some sort of compromise between these two versions can exist. The question is which version provides the most opportunities for the ST when running an Anarch Free State chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-19-2025, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T21:21:03-07:00","id":1550256,"title":"","content":"I always liked San Francisco, though I prefer the Palatine version described in earlier sourcebooks. I do like your analogy to Casablanca. Great movie. I saw it in college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T12:10:38-07:00","id":1550277,"title":"","content":"It is easy to say that San Francisco should be some kind of city of intrigue where anarchs and elders can meet and plot. However, I think it becomes complicated when trying to explain to PCs why the anarchs just don't attack and take San Francisco. That would eliminate any potential threat after all, and the benefits of places like the Vampire Club seems nebulous.<br /> <br /> One is to emphasize the power of the elders in San Francisco and the support the Kindred there have for them. They did after all defeat the initial anarch attempt to take the city back in 1945. Of course, the city of San Francisco is now vastly different in 1994 than it was in 1945. In many ways I think people would assume San Francisco should be more amenable or welcoming to the anarchs since the sixties. Of course, Kindred there may contrast that with how the Free States are actually governed. <br /> <br /> Non-Brujah might very much fear the Brujah clan, and we can make it that San Francisco is not a very good place for the Brujah. Other clans make sure of that. Yeah, local Brujah vampires may get dissatisfied, but instead of staying in the city and causing trouble, they might just go down to Los Angeles anyway. The other clans strengthen their hold over the city. Not only are the Ventrue, Toreador, and Tremere committed to the status quo, so are the Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Malkavian.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that the actual governance of the Free States don't attract many Kindred who might otherwise be sympathetic to the anarchs. It's all well and good to shout about freedom. It's another thing to see no personal safety, lots of Kindred dying, open cannibalism, and gang warfare. They are close enough to the Free States to have a lot of good information. Anarchs they once befriended are now long destroyed, and they don't particularly like how the experiment has turned out.<br /> <br /> So the LA Anarchs just don't see San Francisco as a tempting target. They don't have local allies that could help them. The elders there are powerful. Attempts to take the city would bring Petrodon and his archons to the city immediately. To take the city would take a great effort.<br /> <br /> Now because the Free States are very much a &quot;do whatever you want&quot;, there's nothing preventing some charismatic anarch from convincing others to do it anyway. Nobody is going to stop them. However, I think in practice, there isn't an anarch leader who could convince a critical mass of anarchs to do so. Of course, MacNeil could do it, but we can easily say that he personally sees the arrangements of the 1946 Conclave to be beneficial and honors it. He's not going to stop any other anarch from leading an attack, but he won't participate himself. The other major anarch leaders probably have their own reasons to do the same. So that leaves only lesser stature anarch leaders who would want to attack it.<br /> <br /> I imagine some do, and that there have been various low scale anarch attacks in the fifty or so years between 1945-1994. It's just a quick way to get anarchs killed. Vannevar Thomas and the primogen don't particularly like that, but they don't hold it against MacNeil and the others. If they did, they might risk him leading the next attack. Better to just deal with the troublemakers as they come and maintain the status quo.<br /> <br /> Letting these foolhardy anarchs kill themselves strangely doesn't seem to diminish MacNeil's standing. Why? It's because the other anarchs know MacNeil is doing things to help the anarch council. He leads the Anarch Council and provides help to anarchs in other domains. A general needs to make strategic and tactical decisions. If he and the council decided it's better for the movement to leave San Francisco alone and support efforts elsewhere, it's something other anarchs can accept or tolerate even if they disagree with. Thankfully we do have lots of canon examples where the anarchs do receive help and even successes at places. I imagine to the vast majority of anarchs, &quot;MacNeil knows best&quot; and the obvious support of other anarchs like Salvador Garcia is enough that most don't question the decision not to invade. And for those anarchs who do complain, the problem for them is simple. If they care so much, why not do it themselves? Those who do, get killed. Those who don't look like blowhards and discredit themselves. In either case, they cause no more problems for MacNeil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T16:41:56-07:00","id":1550281,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> just to clarify. Is your San Francisco chronicle set in 1994? Is that because you don\u2019t like the worldview of the V5 games? Or did you just want to set it thirty years in the past like a historical chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 04-19-2025, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T01:25:17-07:00","id":1550283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550281#post1550281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> just to clarify. Is your San Francisco chronicle set in 1994? Is that because you don\u2019t like the worldview of the V5 games? Or did you just want to set it thirty years in the past like a historical chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't be running a San Francisco chronicle per se. I'll be running a chronicle set in the Anarch Free State of Los Angeles which I expect will involve San Francisco to some degree. I mention 1994 because that is the year of the Los Angeles By Night sourcebook. I'll probably begin the chronicle in 1992 right after the riots. I choose this because 1) it allows me to use various early edition sourcebooks, and 2) I do like historical chronicles that allow me to progress time and better balance XP versus character improvement over time. I am still in preparation stages, but the game will likely begin in August this year.<br /> <br /> I am not a fan of metaplot and do not like either the metaplot changes of the setting of Revised or V5. This does not mean I dislike everything those editions did, but I tend to default to 1e and early 2e canon and only selectively use &quot;innovations&quot; introduced later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T04:08:46-07:00","id":1550297,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that San Francisco was almost certainly the fallback position/refuge for Kindred who escaped the Second Anarch Revolt - in other words some of the toughest, luckiest and most resourceful vampires on the Left Coast, all of them possessed of a powerful disinclination to roll over as the Anarchs roll in, with a well-regarded, well-entrenched and successful Prince to rally the defences.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another is that, like West Berlin, the city of San Francisco is strategically and politically-valuable to the Camarilla to a degree that suggests they would further reinforce local defences to the point where seizing the city would be a protracted and presumably painful process (No matter how certain an eventual Anarch victory may be).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, San Francisco tying down a significant portion of Free State forces whilst the Camarilla (or worse, the Sabbat) hit the weakened Anarch Frontier would be a potentially-nasty strategic situation for the Staters (Especially if Camarilla relicts or infiltrators in the Free States made some trouble).<br /> <br /> <br /> (I almost forgot to suggest that having an outpost of the Ivory Tower still standing tall in Anarch territory would have been - and may continue to be - valuable to Camarilla propagandists, a rare victory in the ongoing humiliations of the Second Anarch Revolt).<br /> <br /> <br /> Another point to consider is that Anarch Idealogues (Especially native Californians made since the Summer of Love) might be entirely convinced that the counterculture traditions in San Francisco and the Bay Area, coupled to the Essential Rightness of the Anarch Cause, means that it\u2019s impossible for the Camarilla to hold out in San Francisco over the long haul - and therefore shout down or knock down anyone who calls for Direct Action, so that the Free States can finally present the world a Triumph of the Anarch Ideology (Not just win another punch-up with teeth), representing the Sect achieving it\u2019s full maturity. <br /> <br /> Also, the \u2018Counterculture\u2019 Anarchs might be deeply reluctant to turn their old stamping grounds into a war zone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, it seems reasonable to suggest that the Free States have more to gain by holding San Francisco a hostage to fortune than by swallowing up yet another city - it\u2019s easy to imagine the current quid pro quo which leaves a single Camarilla city near the heart of the Free States being arrived at after concessions and compromises that probably explain the \u2018Palatine\u2019 status of the local Prince &amp; Primogen: by allowing these individuals unprecedented power to negotiate with their neighbours, the Inner Circle of the Camarilla also allow them to take any blame that might attach to said compromises and concessions - allowing the Ivory Tower itself to stand tall and retain the option of disavowing any of the Palatinate concessions at discretion).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Free States leadership have a nice, vulnerable Camarilla sore spot to poke when they want to send a message without risking their assets in Enemy Territory (and hopefully extract more concessions or score points in the ongoing Cold War situation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T04:12:13-07:00","id":1550298,"title":"","content":"This doesn\u2019t even consider the Wild Card presented by the l Garou population on the Bay Area: given the local Caern is one of the eponymous CAERNS: PLACES OF POWER, it seems unlikely that a massed vampire offensive in the region would be either welcomed with open arms or ignored (and nobody sane wants a three way brawl in which one way leads you right at THE Combat Monsters of the classic World of Darkness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T04:16:03-07:00","id":1550299,"title":"","content":"Also also, given KINDRED: THE EMBRACED and CHARMED were both put together by Spelling Television, the odds of there NOT being at least one alarmingly powerful coven of sexy female mages in the local San Francisco are absolutely minuscule (Adding another wild card to the local strategic situation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T15:25:59-07:00","id":1550304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550298#post1550298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This doesn\u2019t even consider the Wild Card presented by the l Garou population on the Bay Area: given the local Caern is one of the eponymous CAERNS: PLACES OF POWER, it seems unlikely that a massed vampire offensive in the region would be either welcomed with open arms or ignored (and nobody sane wants a three way brawl in which one way leads you right at THE Combat Monsters of the classic World of Darkness).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Children of Gaia caern in C:PP is &quot;only&quot; rank three and set north of the city in Muir Woods National Monument. So most vampires would likely easily avoid that. However, that chapter also tells us that there are Bone Gnawers in San Francisco itself (mostly Golden Gate Park) with a hidden caern somewhere, and Glass Walkers in Silicon Valley also with their own caern. If we imagine that many of the kinfolk of all three tribes are in groups that would make &quot;natural&quot; anarchs if they were to become vampires, then the local Garou might prevent a lot of vampires from coming out of these groups in order to prevent their kinfolk from being preyed upon. It might be something the Camarilla elders in town learned, and the anarchs from LA don't. So it might lead to a lot of destruction of unknowing anarchs who hope to use that population as a potential fifth column.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the Garou here getting information from LA based Garou who tell them that the vampire population of LA are particularly corrupt because of the Setite Temples, general decadence of Hollywood and the media industry, and the higher than normal presence of Kindred criminals and cannibals, and the local Garou might very well prefer their local bunch than newcomers. Those three tribes are also the tribes most prone to come to some sort of accommodation with individual vampires so they may actually want to make a distinction. Yeah, the local Leeches are bad, but better than having them replaced by those in LA.<br /> <br /> It could be interesting for some of this to lodge into the information known to the LA vampires as a general rule like &quot;Avoid hippies, homeless, homosexuals, and hackers.&quot; That eliminates most of the obvious &quot;radical politics&quot; groups that could be recruited as either childer, herds, or allies. Maybe there is even some legend like Vannevar Thomas has blood bound Lupines that kill anarchs there. He doesn't, but the anarchs might think that based on any increased frequency of encounters with Lupines there (compared to LA).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T00:04:18-07:00","id":1550313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550299#post1550299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also also, given KINDRED: THE EMBRACED and CHARMED were both put together by Spelling Television, the odds of there NOT being at least one alarmingly powerful coven of sexy female mages in the local San Francisco are absolutely minuscule (Adding another wild card to the local strategic situation).</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally don't consider Mage in my Vampire chronicles. I tend to rely on Sorcerer for any magickal people interacting with vampires as I consider true Mages acting on a level much higher than most vampires in a chronicle will ever be at. However, I might very well create a small sorcerer coven (pseudo-Verbena) based on the Charmed characters in SF. That show was incredibly popular when I played in LARP, and my players were all in that same age bracket (we're old folks). They might get a small kick out of it. Non-trivial chance they are named Prue, Piper, Phoebe, and Paige. I'll reserve any LA sorcerers to be based on Buffy instead.<br /> <br /> But like with all living mortal to vampire interactions, I would need to give an immense amount of thought of how they would protect themselves from vampire treachery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T04:12:03-07:00","id":1550315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550304#post1550304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Children of Gaia caern in C:PP is &quot;only&quot; rank three and set north of the city in Muir Woods National Monument. So most vampires would likely easily avoid that. However, that chapter also tells us that there are Bone Gnawers in San Francisco itself (mostly Golden Gate Park) with a hidden caern somewhere, and Glass Walkers in Silicon Valley also with their own caern. If we imagine that many of the kinfolk of all three tribes are in groups that would make &quot;natural&quot; anarchs if they were to become vampires, then the local Garou might prevent a lot of vampires from coming out of these groups in order to prevent their kinfolk from being preyed upon. It might be something the Camarilla elders in town learned, and the anarchs from LA don't. So it might lead to a lot of destruction of unknowing anarchs who hope to use that population as a potential fifth column.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the Garou here getting information from LA based Garou who tell them that the vampire population of LA are particularly corrupt because of the Setite Temples, general decadence of Hollywood and the media industry, and the higher than normal presence of Kindred criminals and cannibals, and the local Garou might very well prefer their local bunch than newcomers. Those three tribes are also the tribes most prone to come to some sort of accommodation with individual vampires so they may actually want to make a distinction. Yeah, the local Leeches are bad, but better than having them replaced by those in LA.<br /> <br /> It could be interesting for some of this to lodge into the information known to the LA vampires as a general rule like &quot;Avoid hippies, homeless, homosexuals, and hackers.&quot; That eliminates most of the obvious &quot;radical politics&quot; groups that could be recruited as either childer, herds, or allies. Maybe there is even some legend like Vannevar Thomas has blood bound Lupines that kill anarchs there. He doesn't, but the anarchs might think that based on any increased frequency of encounters with Lupines there (compared to LA).</div> </div> </div> </div> The fact that the Sept of the Western Eye includes Uktena amongst it\u2019s members helps to make it even more potentially-dangerous: if nothing else, an insult to or assault on the caern would risk angering TWO Tribes with one stroke (and Elder Brother\u2019s insatiable curiosity and sorcerous versatility make a nice compliment to the Children\u2019s knack for making friends &amp; close attention to humanity).<br /> <br /> It does amuse me to imagine Prince Vannevar Thomas getting wind of these urban legends and ruefully recalling that one time he had to fight a \u2018Lone Wolf\u2019 in single combat.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s such a thing as a tame Lupine, he hasn\u2019t met them yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T04:26:12-07:00","id":1550316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550313#post1550313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally don't consider Mage in my Vampire chronicles. I tend to rely on Sorcerer for any magickal people interacting with vampires as I consider true Mages acting on a level much higher than most vampires in a chronicle will ever be at. However, I might very well create a small sorcerer coven (pseudo-Verbena) based on the Charmed characters in SF. That show was incredibly popular when I played in LARP, and my players were all in that same age bracket (we're old folks). They might get a small kick out of it. Non-trivial chance they are named Prue, Piper, Phoebe, and Paige. I'll reserve any LA sorcerers to be based on Buffy instead.<br /> <br /> But like with all living mortal to vampire interactions, I would need to give an immense amount of thought of how they would protect themselves from vampire treachery.</div> </div> </div> </div> - WAGS FINGER - <br /> <br /> For shame, sir, this simply isn\u2019t the proper way to do pastiche - at the very least one should change the names for the sake of allowing one\u2019s lawyers to dance the seven veils when the copyright lawyers come calling.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I respectfully suggest the names Heather, Holly and Hazel Spelling, along with their half-sister Sabrina Hart (Yes, that last one is even more of a shameless in-joke, but I like the idea of mirroring the other sister\u2019s initials and that SH might well be the only genuine Mage amongst the set).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for what keeps them from being vampired, one could given them support from a friendly Wraith (A pastiche of Leo Wyatt - possibly call him \u2018Felix\u2019* and make a running joke about the uninformed assuming that he\u2019s the house cat, though more astute observers may recognise that the pussycat in question is a Queen and not a Tom.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>\u2019Felix Thompson\u2019 is a shameless, shameless pun and I make no apologies for</i> it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, given that \u2018Cole\u2019 was originally based on Angel (from BUFFY THE VAMPIRE SLAYER) it might be appropriate to make his pastiche one of the Kindred, rather than a Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T18:03:06-07:00","id":1550328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550316#post1550316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For shame, sir, this simply isn\u2019t the proper way to do pastiche</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never actually seen even one episode of Charmed so I can't do a pastiche of it! All I know are the names of three of the actresses. I had to look up their character names on Wikipedia. My players are probably the same way although one is younger so she may have watched it growing up. So the only way to reference it, if I wanted, would be to use the names. Other than Sabrina the Teenage Witch, I have no idea who are the other characters you are talking about.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> As I explained earlier, there's some non-alignment with earlier references to San Francisco and the Free States to what is in LABN. The references to San Francisco there treat it like any other Camarilla domain. Still, more civilized anarchs might visit the Vampire Club. There's various reasons why they might.<br /> <br /> First, the club has an &quot;open door&quot; policy. Any Kindred &quot;in relatively good standing&quot; is welcome. I'd take that to mean not an obvious killer or cannibal to other Kindred. Whatever the definition, it has to extend to most anarchs. I'm not sure how that is different from any kind of Elysium, but A World of Darkness 1e was written <i>very</i> early, and at this time &quot;elysium&quot; as a concept might just have been a local thing associated with Lodin in Chicago. Now it'd just be easier to say it's just a recognized Elysium. However, beyond that, I'd emphasize the welcoming nature of its owner, Sebastian Melmoth, who sincerely just wants people to enjoy themselves, including Caitiffs.<br /> <br /> Second, its general manager, Tex R. Cainen, was sired by an LA anarch (back in 1916 who was destroyed in 1921) and was somehow involved in the 1944 uprising against Don Sebastian. Whether or not he counts as an actual anarch, he certainly has some amount of street cred with MacNeil, Garcia, Fortier, and others. Any visiting anarchs from LA are probably told to see him and not cause trouble. The ST could probably also some backstory about he and Melmoth participated in the 1946 Conclave held at the Vampire Club and helped negotiate the &quot;Palatine Treaty&quot; that gave it &quot;unheard of autonomy&quot; and seemed to make peace with the local anarchs. Like a lot of things, I wish we had more details on what exactly this did and how this kept the peace, but whatever the ST decides, it can give greater weight to Tex's reputation among the anarchs.<br /> <br /> Third, I'd probably make some high sect status anarchs regular attendees just to give it some bona fides. I wouldn't make it any of the Kindred on the Anarch Council or the major gang leaders. Whatever the major promises or reputation, there's too much risk for them to attend someplace they do not control themselves. Not saying they never have shown up or never would, but it'd best to make any appearances rare and surprising. Nor anyone too disruptive like Smiling Jack or someone on the Red List like Germaine.<br /> <br /> However, we do have good candidates. Crispus Attucks is one. He's a frequent traveler who has made a lot of contacts. He's a noteworthy historical figure that some Kindred might want to preserve simply because. And despite his physical power, he knows how to behave. He certainly has the anarch status that would cause many to respect a place he shows up at. Amethyst might make an interesting attendee. While important locally, she doesn't have a reputation outside LA. She travels frequently, and as a Caitiff she has both Melmoth's sympathies and would provide proof that he treats the clanless well. She has good social skills and due to her prior history of being a consort to the Prince of Baltimore, she would get along well there. Since I don't have Louis Fortier showing up himself, one of his brides would be good. I'd pick Elena Gutierrez as she's his agent to the outside world including other vampires. Someone like Therese Voerman would also make sense.<br /> <br /> One or more of the Brujah Idealists could also attend, but their status would only be important to other Brujah who respected their clan prestige, not as members of the anarchs. Likewise I might have the Vignes couple show up on occasion if an event was particular to their tastes, but despite any local respect the LA anarchs might have for him, I'd doubt he has any real pull with them. But the attendance of more local anarchs would make the Vampire Club more attractive.<br /> <br /> I'll probably add a few more to this list of characters I created for my chronicle. Of course, if I want to use this as a setting element, I need to find a way to include the PCs on this list as well. I'll probably figure out a good &quot;quest giver&quot; who would ask the PCs to travel there to conduct business on her behalf. They'd then see some LA characters and also introduce local San Francisco Kindred (like Countess D'adhemar) that have relevance to the chronicle as well.<br /> <br /> This is also where I'd have any anarch sympathizers within the Camarilla from other domains show up. If I want Modius from Gary, Inyanga from Chicago, or Edward Scott from Milwaukee to show up for example, I'd have them travel here and then meet up with anarch reps from LA. I normally don't like to insert or name drop canon characters into a chronicle, but here it makes some sense. If I ever need to use an Assamite, it'll be Badr al-Budr from Milwaukee By Night as she mentions San Francisco as one of the places she's been hired.<br /> <br /> <br /> Many anarchs won't like the atmosphere of the Vampire Club which is still dominated by classic Toreador salon culture. It's main guests are still Ventrue and Toreador. However, we're also told many anarchs prefer nightspots like the &quot;I-Beam&quot; and &quot;DV-8&quot; so I'll just have them be hangouts by the local San Francisco anarchs, or be the place that visiting anarch companions would visit while waiting for the person they are escorting to leave the Vampire Club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T12:22:31-07:00","id":1550344,"title":"","content":"\u201cI've never actually seen even one episode of Charmed so I can't do a pastiche of it! All I know are the names of three of the actresses. I had to look up their character names on Wikipedia. My players are probably the same way although one is younger so she may have watched it growing up. So the only way to reference it, if I wanted, would be to use the names. Other than Sabrina the Teenage Witch, I have no idea who are the other characters you are talking about.\u201d<br /> <br /> Try TV TROPES - all the information with double the Nerd Goodies (Beware though, TV TROPES <i>is</i> an addictive experience).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019d best cash money that at least one or more of Tara\u2019s brood is a fairly regular visitor to the Vampire Club in San Francisco (The Baron of San Diego needed to establish a back door line of communication with the Ivory Tower somewhere, after all); I\u2019d also bet cash money that \u2018Task Force Ex\u2019 member are the Anarchs least likely to risk a trip to San Fran (Given that unlike quite a number of other Anarchs, they\u2019re not just rebels but defectors).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T19:04:11-07:00","id":1550355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550344#post1550344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I\u2019d best cash money that at least one or more of Tara\u2019s brood is a fairly regular visitor to the Vampire Club in San Francisco (The Baron of San Diego needed to establish a back door line of communication with the Ivory Tower somewhere, after all)</div> </div> </div> </div>A trusted friend might have initially made contact with someone there, but it was probably to discuss some plausible deniability topic like experiences fighting the Sabbat or something. Just enough to make contact and set up an alternate avenue for secret discussion. Said person probably showed up several times before and afterward just to make it seem normal they would be at the club, but that kind of talk absolutely needs to be done elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tLmvjE674k\" data-code=\"5tLmvjE674k\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5tLmvjE674k/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> In situations like this, you want to normalize some kind of casual contact, but not risk having it be seen as suspicious. It might be more than just a fine line, but it is still a narrow corridor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L6G0VxscwqE\" data-code=\"L6G0VxscwqE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/L6G0VxscwqE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550344#post1550344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d also bet cash money that \u2018Task Force Ex\u2019 member are the Anarchs least likely to risk a trip to San Fran (Given that unlike quite a number of other Anarchs, they\u2019re not just rebels but defectors).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Geduld or anyone close to him could ever show up. Less that Geduld defected and stopped being Lodin's spy in LA, and more because as a Ventrue baron, he absolutely cannot risk being seen in LA as someone who might be a Prince in waiting. Imagine the rumors if he even bumped into Vannevar Thomas once at the Vampire Club. If he absolutely needs something done at the club, he probably asks someone not from his gang that he trusts to go there and represent him. Preferably a Brujah or Gangrel with good sect status who like him for whatever reason, and could vouch that there was nothing scandalous discussed. At least, that is how I would run it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LwsgYoahVVs\" data-code=\"LwsgYoahVVs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LwsgYoahVVs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T14:50:59-07:00","id":1550366,"title":"","content":"<b>Suggestion: Why Vannevar survived as Prince of San Fransisco</b><br /> <br /> My interpretation of San Fransisco for the World of Darkness was that Vannevar Thomas was someone the Anarchs loathed to a great deal because he represented something that was an ideological challenge to their ranks: The Prince no one really hated. I think this was actually canon for awhile.<br /> <br /> While about 200 years old and an Elder even by European standards, albeit barely, Vannevar had spent most of his time in San Fransisco as a much younger vampire. Frequently, like Lodin, he was actually finding himself the underdog against much nastier vampires. As such, the older vampires in San Fransisco considered him an improvement over the previous princes and the younger vampires generally didn't have quite as big a collection of the atrocities to point to as other domains. One might argue he was comparatively a soft touch.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that Vannevar Thomas was a &quot;good&quot; person or a weak prince. He still staked and burned people who threatened the Masquerade and played the games that Kindred do. However, the Second Anarch Revolt stopped around San Fransisco simply because of him understanding two things.<br /> <br /> 1:] Vannevar understood that while he could not be loved and feared by all Kindred, he was certainly not HATED.<br /> <br /> 2:] He was able to rally the Kindred of San Fransisco to believe the Anarchs coming to &quot;free them&quot; intended to do so in order to seize the locals domains. Which had the benefit of being true.<br /> <br /> 3:] Both the Eastern Kindred and Sabbat had their designs on the city and were willing to repulse the Anarchs alongside Vannevar. Ironically, he'd deal with both in <i>Dark Prince</i>.<br /> <br /> If I were to make an interesting scene, I imagien Jeremy MacNeil meeting Vannevar and finding that Vannevar was NOT a Camarilla loyalist himself. Indeed, he'd almost been overthrown several times by the Justicars and happy to cut a backroom deal with the Anarchs. <i>Prince of the City</i> notably makes it clear that he was almost overthrown multiple times for the Archons pick.<br /> <br /> This actually becomes the canon end of Vannevar's reign as he gets himself replaced for being too soft on the Anarchs and Thin Bloods. Probably because, like the prince of Berlin, Vannevar understands the Prince better than the petty tyrants under the increasingly mad Inner Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T19:05:20-07:00","id":1550369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550366#post1550366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation of San Fransisco for the World of Darkness was that Vannevar Thomas was someone the Anarchs loathed to a great deal because he represented something that was an ideological challenge to their ranks: The Prince no one really hated.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting angle to use. Explains why that domain is overwhelming in favor of his rule. Of course, even a united domain still needs to hold out over dozens, perhaps even a hundred anarchs who could march there. But in terms of the mid-forties, many of the anarchs who might have marched off to San Francisco could either have perished during the fighting, or were happy with the turf they already grabbed for themselves, meaning those who were still willing to fight in San Francisco by this time did not have any numerical advantage. Thus the willingness to accept a compromise in 1946.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550366#post1550366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both the Eastern Kindred and Sabbat had their designs on the city and were willing to repulse the Anarchs alongside Vannevar. Ironically, he'd deal with both in <i>Dark Prince</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that mentioned at? That the local Sabbat were willing to assist Vannevar defeat the anarchs means they saw MacNeil and company as the much greater threat at the time. Of course, we must also remember that the Sabbat in 1945/1946 was pre-Third Sabbat Civil War, and was somewhat of a different animal than what occurred before. I would think Loyalists would be much more likely to work with the anarchs, and then perhaps try to get their support in the next civil war. So maybe it more old school Lasombra who saw that threat and decided thwarting the anarchs (not helping Prince Vannevar of course, they'd never do that...) was more of a priority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550366#post1550366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to make an interesting scene, I imagien Jeremy MacNeil meeting Vannevar and finding that Vannevar was NOT a Camarilla loyalist himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible MacNeil and other LA anarch leaders attended that 1946 Conclave. If he didn't meet Vannevar directly, than someone like Fortier might have and told MacNeil that Vannever was someone they could deal with unlike Don Sebastian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550366#post1550366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, he'd almost been overthrown several times by the Justicars and happy to cut a backroom deal with the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the more interesting distinctions between anarchs are those that simply want to take down the local prince or princes in general, and those who see the Inner Circle and the Justicars as their primary opponent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550366#post1550366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Prince of the City</i> notably makes it clear that he was almost overthrown multiple times for the Archons pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read the actual game fiction that is really our main source on San Francisco, or at least something based on the original intention of the first writers. By the time that White Wolf game fiction came out, I had already stopped reading gaming fiction. I just did not find their quality good enough to keep going. So it's good to hear about the setting from someone who did, as for this purpose at least, there'll be some good information there likely not captured on some wiki.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T04:57:43-07:00","id":1550377,"title":"","content":"My read on Prince Vannevar Thomas is that he\u2019s a genuine moderate: he\u2019s not old enough or deep enough in the Old Boy network* to be heart-and-blood Camarilla, but he\u2019s too invested in good order and the quiet life to really favour the Anarchs; as for the Sabbat, I suspect he prefers to keep his distance.<br /> <br /> Therefore Prince Thomas is here to do business and that business preserves the Balance of Power (Which, at least in San Francisco during the Age of the Free States, is very much to the Camarilla\u2019s favour - although I suspect the Inner Council has debated that point a time or three, with no firm agreement between the factions).<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>From what we can gather, his Sire lived as a Caitiff and a vicious one at that, it was only after decades as a vampire that Thomas got in touch with the Texas Camarilla, so it\u2019s easy to imagine there being something of a question mark over his lineage - worse, he never went through the Agoge, so his Ventrue credentials are somewhat in question on that score as </i>well.<br /> <br /> <br /> In all honesty I would suggest making San Francisco, not Los Angeles, Sebastian LaCroix\u2019s home base during the early 1990s - he\u2019d be far more at home as the Clan Ventrue\u2019s eye on Vannevar Thomas and the Camarilla\u2019s occasional messenger to the Free States than as a Kindred with specific ambitions towards Los Angeles (Which makes it all the more hilariously apparent that his being made Prince of the latter city was a backhanded compliment and very possibly a reward for services rendered that also worked as a punishment for undermining a fellow Ventrue).<br /> <br /> Heck, there might even be a steady stream of hungry Ventrue into San Francisco, looking into how Prince Vannevar Thomas does things and arguing over whether he\u2019s a proper Ventrue, not just a <i>successful</i> Ventrue (More than one of them has even left the city alive afterwards, although not necessarily of their own free choice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T05:12:52-07:00","id":1550378,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I remain fascinated by the question of whether it might be worth smuggling a few nods to KINDRED: THE EMBRACED into San Francisco circa 1990s - if only as a TV show that actually aired in the WORLD OF DARKNESS and was accurate enough to be killed on sight.*<br /> <br /> Possibly literally, this being VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>I tend to assume that the TV characters would be fictionalised versions of actual San Fran kindred or at least drawn from recognisable \u2018types\u2019 and that some of the incidents would be true to the local secret history, even if the show\u2019s version of vampirism doesn\u2019t really follow the VtM rules.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m assuming that - in the World of Darkness - might well have caused something of a diplomatic incident between LA and San Francisco (Possibly with the Camarilla being Dangerously Patient with Prince Thomas and the latter making some pointed enquiries around the entertainment industry - this being headquartered in the Free States, Drama could well ensue if the parties involved get a little <i>too</i> in deep).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll bet you could a Vampire Club session out if the challenge of deep-sixing the show and working out who sprang the original leak (Also various NPCs preening or snarling over their fictionalised counterparts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Addition of italics. 04-25-2025, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T07:07:40-07:00","id":1550380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550369#post1550369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting angle to use. Explains why that domain is overwhelming in favor of his rule. Of course, even a united domain still needs to hold out over dozens, perhaps even a hundred anarchs who could march there. But in terms of the mid-forties, many of the anarchs who might have marched off to San Francisco could either have perished during the fighting, or were happy with the turf they already grabbed for themselves, meaning those who were still willing to fight in San Francisco by this time did not have any numerical advantage. Thus the willingness to accept a compromise in 1946.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Dark Prince shows Vannevar as scheming and cruel as any Ventrue but oddly enough that's the perspective of the main character and everyone else acts like he's being an excessive asshole (which he is). Prince of the City is from Vannevar's perspective and the irony is that he really is trying to be as even handed as he can without looking weak. He's not quite American Ned Stark but he's a lot more respectable a leader than Saint Croix or Lodin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is that mentioned at? That the local Sabbat were willing to assist Vannevar defeat the anarchs means they saw MacNeil and company as the much greater threat at the time. Of course, we must also remember that the Sabbat in 1945/1946 was pre-Third Sabbat Civil War, and was somewhat of a different animal than what occurred before. I would think Loyalists would be much more likely to work with the anarchs, and then perhaps try to get their support in the next civil war. So maybe it more old school Lasombra who saw that threat and decided thwarting the anarchs (not helping Prince Vannevar of course, they'd never do that...) was more of a priority. </div> </div> </div>It should be noted when I refer to the Sabbat, I don't mean the openly Sword of Caine ones that Vannevar would exterminate. But Dark Prince has the Sabbat heavily infiltrated the city under the former Prince of the City (who is implied to be Aztec Lasombra) that was overthrown by Vannevar's predecessor. They're a bunch of murderous Satanists and evil doers as Sabbat are but are ostensibly supporting Vannevar until they can overthrow him.<br /> <br /> The Eastern Kindred are also surprisingly there as &quot;The Family&quot; is a bunch of non-Clan Kindred (that are still vampires) and plan to take over the city but have been supporting him against the Anarchs as well.<br /> <br /> Typical 1st Edition Vampire politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the more interesting distinctions between anarchs are those that simply want to take down the local prince or princes in general, and those who see the Inner Circle and the Justicars as their primary opponent. </div> </div> </div>One of the Choice of Games novels, Parliament of Shadows, had the Methuselah prince of the city reveal that the Camarilla has been undermining Princes since its beginning and trying to replace competent capable princes with the love of their subjects (be it via bribes or Disciplines or other means--he's not being a romantic) with lickspittles and toadies. The Camarilla preferring petty tyrants to people who might build their own Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It's not anywhere else but I thought it was an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never read the actual game fiction that is really our main source on San Francisco, or at least something based on the original intention of the first writers. By the time that White Wolf game fiction came out, I had already stopped reading gaming fiction. I just did not find their quality good enough to keep going. So it's good to hear about the setting from someone who did, as for this purpose at least, there'll be some good information there likely not captured on some wiki. </div> </div> </div>I recommend picking up both novels as it shows how a lot of later ideas were already there. They're also on Kindle and in reprints now thanks to Crossroad Press. Audiobook too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T19:14:26-07:00","id":1550389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550378#post1550378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I remain fascinated by the question of whether it might be worth smuggling a few nods to KINDRED: THE EMBRACED into San Francisco circa 1990s - if only as a TV show that actually aired in the WORLD OF DARKNESS and was accurate enough to be killed on sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there will be such a TV show, it's based on the Black Dog Game Factory game which in my chronicles is not part of PENTEX, but is part of a Wyrm conspiracy because Jack Chick is right about these kinds of games.<br /> <br /> I do hold that as part of trend of portraying vampires not as horrible monsters needing to be destroyed, but tragic, misunderstood, romantic figures needing and giving love in mass media, such things are part of a long term conspiracy by vampires to groom humanity into being complacent and willing vessels and collaborators. Normally its the Inner Circle behind such things, but the Free States complicates things in LA. However, there are Brujah in LA interested in a building a new &quot;Carthage&quot;, and they'll pick up the slack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T19:25:41-07:00","id":1550390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550380#post1550380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prince of the City is from Vannevar's perspective and the irony is that he really is trying to be as even handed as he can without looking weak. He's not quite American Ned Stark but he's a lot more respectable a leader than Saint Croix or Lodin.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very much the default of a lot of PCs so I'm not surprised that is how an author wanted to portray him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550380#post1550380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Eastern Kindred are also surprisingly there as &quot;The Family&quot; is a bunch of non-Clan Kindred (that are still vampires) and plan to take over the city but have been supporting him against the Anarchs as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how I want to handle the eastern Kindred. I never really liked it as a setting element because even though China was not well known to Europe, there was lots of contact with India and the Middle East which was also part of the Camarilla. The idea that such Kindred were unknown and mysterious never made sense to me. However, it is part of the original lore so I'll probably go with it. I won't be using Kindred of the East though. I'll use original Gaki and Bushi plus actual folklore and probably handwave a lot of powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550380#post1550380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Choice of Games novels, Parliament of Shadows, had the Methuselah prince of the city reveal that the Camarilla has been undermining Princes since its beginning and trying to replace competent capable princes with the love of their subjects (be it via bribes or Disciplines or other means--he's not being a romantic) with lickspittles and toadies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The conflicts between the Princes and the Inner Circle over ultimate authority was there in the first corebook I think, definitely in the second corebook. But that distinction was often overlooked, and more or less forgotten when Revised became all about sect wars between the Camarilla and Sabbat. The idea of outright replacing competent princes for pawns they'll directly administer makes no sense though. There is already too much to be done to do such micromanaging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550380#post1550380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend picking up both novels as it shows how a lot of later ideas were already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That won't be happening. While I do like to perform some amount archaeology, and I'm sure they'll be easy reads, I have zero interest other than a Cliff's Notes version of how they presented San Francisco.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T11:36:49-07:00","id":1550399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550389#post1550389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there will be such a TV show, it's based on the Black Dog Game Factory game which in my chronicles is not part of PENTEX, but is part of a Wyrm conspiracy because Jack Chick is right about these kinds of games.<br /> <br /> I do hold that as part of trend of portraying vampires not as horrible monsters needing to be destroyed, but tragic, misunderstood, romantic figures needing and giving love in mass media, such things are part of a long term conspiracy by vampires to groom humanity into being complacent and willing vessels and collaborators. Normally its the Inner Circle behind such things, but the Free States complicates things in LA. However, there are Brujah in LA interested in a building a new &quot;Carthage&quot;, and they'll pick up the slack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now imagining a weird and wild plot by Christopher the 5th Generation Toreador who is the guy behind Aaron spelling (and sire of Isaac from Bloodlines). Christopher developed yet another one of his &quot;crushes&quot; on Vannevar Thomas and created the Kindred: The Embraced equivalent, Revenant: The Creation, or whatever, and it was something that included a huge number of barely concealed parodies of the main cast.<br /> <br /> Julian Luna/Marcus Sun: The Vannevar Thomas pastiche that is the good hearted Prince who does way more of the dirty work than expected.<br /> <br /> Lilly Langtree; The Prince's Toreador mistress.<br /> <br /> Daedelus: His Sheriff and so on.<br /> <br /> So much so the Camarilla believed this was actually Vannevar's vanity project and removed him from the Princedom for a gross breach of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Hilarious Real Life Matter: White Wolf actually used Vannevar Thomas (even though he'd already been removed as Prince in canon) as part of a marketing stunt for Bloodlines. On the website, Lucita and Vannevar argue about Troika making Bloodlines with the latter saying it'll make any leaks about the Masquerade look ridiculous while Lucita suggests it'll give way too much info to those already in the know.<br /> <br /> I wish it was still online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-26-2025, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T11:03:05-07:00","id":1550409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550377#post1550377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty I would suggest making San Francisco, not Los Angeles, Sebastian LaCroix\u2019s home base during the early 1990s - he\u2019d be far more at home as the Clan Ventrue\u2019s eye on Vannevar Thomas and the Camarilla\u2019s occasional messenger to the Free States than as a Kindred with specific ambitions towards Los Angeles (Which makes it all the more hilariously apparent that his being made Prince of the latter city was a backhanded compliment and very possibly a reward for services rendered that also worked as a punishment for undermining a fellow Ventrue).</div> </div> </div> </div>I might do that. There's not many options to shoehorn LaCroix into sourcebook time period LA itself believably. My idea to make him Fortier's childe from his time in NYC and now on the run wasn't the most elegant solution. Putting him in San Francisco solves various problems. It is a more natural place for him to be, but still close enough that he could potentially play an important role that could see him as Prince should the Camarilla succeed. Assuming the PCs visit the Vampire Club at some point, they could very well run into him there. He might even be a semi-official liaison to visiting anarchs (or any Kindred in general temporarily visiting the Vampire Club) so the local Kindred can keep a watch on them. He doesn't run the place like Melmoth or Cainen, but he's a club regular so he's a fixture for any regular or frequent visitors.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T11:20:38-07:00","id":1550410,"title":"","content":"The conflict between the Kindred of San Francisco and the anarchs is the status of nearby San Jose, the northernmost free state. Ten anarchs, in a single coterie with no baron, defend their turf there. In the description of the barony, it is said they fought off two attempts by Vannevar Thomas to reclaim the area and that currently there is an uneasy truce. In another section, those attacks are described as feints merely intended to keep the anarchs in line, but that Vannevar is planning a serious attempt to actually take back the city. The difference is probably based solely on the perspective of the respective groups.<br /> <br /> One would think San Jose would be important as it is the leading city of Silicon Valley. Controlling that would seem to be an obvious draw for any ambitious Kindred whether Camarilla or anarch. So the lack of any detail or acknowledgment of its significance is surprising in the LABN sourcebook. However, in the World of Darkness, it is entirely probably all the good things are already heavily defended by either lupines (Glasswalkers) or mages (Virtual Adepts or Technocracy). Kindred who get to close just end up disappearing mysteriously so those Kindred who are there end up being the ones involved in much less attractive industries.<br /> <br /> An actual attack by Vannevar that takes San Jose would probably be very destabilizing in any chronicle and lead to a drawn out war between LA and San Francisco that would quickly draw in Petrodon. If the ST wants that, that is all very good. If the ST does not, it would probably be best to not have that event occur, or wait to do it only after some other event that would consume the attention of the LA anarchs. That way either only a relatively small group might attempt to help out as others are too focused on this other event, or by the time the anarchs could decide to march on San Jose, most of them accept it as a fait accompli.<br /> <br /> The issue with the Free State is that it is the definition of mob rule, and mob rule is fickle but passionate. All it takes is one charismatic figure and the mob is off. So Vannevar always risks a confrontation if he takes the offensive. Ironically, the nature of the Brujah means there are lots of charismatic leaders who effectively cancel out each other because everyone has their own passion project.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:22:43-07:00","id":1550445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550389#post1550389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there will be such a TV show, it's based on the Black Dog Game Factory game which in my chronicles is not part of PENTEX, but is part of a Wyrm conspiracy because Jack Chick is right about these kinds of games.<br /> <br /> I do hold that as part of trend of portraying vampires not as horrible monsters needing to be destroyed, but tragic, misunderstood, romantic figures needing and giving love in mass media, such things are part of a long term conspiracy by vampires to groom humanity into being complacent and willing vessels and collaborators. Normally its the Inner Circle behind such things, but the Free States complicates things in LA. However, there are Brujah in LA interested in a building a new &quot;Carthage&quot;, and they'll pick up the slack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know an author - on these very forums and in this very thread, in fact - who built a whole setting based on that idea and what happens after the plan comes to fruition.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I can imagine this as a specifically <i>Toreador</i> plot (Well, Toreador and friends) but not as a scheme the entire Inner Council would sign off on - if only because the nature of the Camarilla strongly suggests that at least some hail from an Age and a social class where acting was a dirty business and actors quite below the salt, but also because the nature of the Masquerade suggests that the Camarilla would be more comfortable with vampire<br /> movies as disinformation to bolster their camouflage than as propaganda building to some sort of reveal, however partial. <br /> <br /> At which point somebody is likely to chime in with \u201cBut the Internet! What about camera phones?\u201d to which I reply \u201cGiven we can barely trust what we see on the Internet without actual Magic and Ancient Conspiracies and multiple millennia of natural selection favouring those who DO NOT poke their nose into things that don\u2019t concern them, I think the secrets of the Camarilla et al are much safer for those who keep them, rather than those who would unmask them.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I do so love to wonder how the Black Dog games differ from their White Wolf counterparts - for one thing I\u2019m fond of the idea that REVENANT technically focuses on all sorts of corporeal undead (Zombies, vampires, mummies) but that vampires somehow seem to get all the best sourcebooks\u2026<br /> <br /> Additionally, it amuses me to imagine the iconic line of \u201cWhere in the World are all the monsters at?\u201d setting books from Black Dog tend to have titles that sound vaguely like TV erotica (Something like DALLAS AFTER DARK for instance).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:31:13-07:00","id":1550446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550410#post1550410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conflict between the Kindred of San Francisco and the anarchs is the status of nearby San Jose, the northernmost free state. Ten anarchs, in a single coterie with no baron, defend their turf there. In the description of the barony, it is said they fought off two attempts by Vannevar Thomas to reclaim the area and that currently there is an uneasy truce. In another section, those attacks are described as feints merely intended to keep the anarchs in line, but that Vannevar is planning a serious attempt to actually take back the city. The difference is probably based solely on the perspective of the respective groups.<br /> <br /> One would think San Jose would be important as it is the leading city of Silicon Valley. Controlling that would seem to be an obvious draw for any ambitious Kindred whether Camarilla or anarch. So the lack of any detail or acknowledgment of its significance is surprising in the LABN sourcebook. However, in the World of Darkness, it is entirely probably all the good things are already heavily defended by either lupines (Glasswalkers) or mages (Virtual Adepts or Technocracy). Kindred who get to close just end up disappearing mysteriously so those Kindred who are there end up being the ones involved in much less attractive industries.<br /> <br /> An actual attack by Vannevar that takes San Jose would probably be very destabilizing in any chronicle and lead to a drawn out war between LA and San Francisco that would quickly draw in Petrodon. If the ST wants that, that is all very good. If the ST does not, it would probably be best to not have that event occur, or wait to do it only after some other event that would consume the attention of the LA anarchs. That way either only a relatively small group might attempt to help out as others are too focused on this other event, or by the time the anarchs could decide to march on San Jose, most of them accept it as a fait accompli.<br /> <br /> The issue with the Free State is that it is the definition of mob rule, and mob rule is fickle but passionate. All it takes is one charismatic figure and the mob is off. So Vannevar always risks a confrontation if he takes the offensive. Ironically, the nature of the Brujah means there are lots of charismatic leaders who effectively cancel out each other because everyone has their own passion project.</div> </div> </div> </div> I love the idea that whilst the Kindred are busy with some<br /> hardcore sect acts, the Garou nation\u2019s more progressive elements are busy making bank (After all, \u2018Silicone Valley\u2019 is exactly the sort of place one would associate with Glass Walkers - not least because the mental image of various vampires trying to convince themselves that no, there really ARE werewolves in the Tech Industry, somehow, despite those lupines being country wolves, what the heck? quite, quite amusing).<br /> <br /> <br /> On a less sardonic note, for some reason the mental image of the San Jose Anarchs being surprisingly Toreador has occurred to me (Mostly because the mental image of a Toreador obsessed with \u2018the art of the deal\u2019 setting out from Hollywood towards Silicone Valley occurred to me and caught my interest), although the Nosferatu love of technology and knack for roughing it suggests they\u2019d arguably be a more plausible pick (Especially since their love of communal living would help explain why there\u2019s no local Baron - most particularly if Vannevar Thomas takes pains to ensure that no such individual emerges in his immediate vicinity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:47:05-07:00","id":1550449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550409#post1550409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might do that. There's not many options to shoehorn LaCroix into sourcebook time period LA itself believably. My idea to make him Fortier's childe from his time in NYC and now on the run wasn't the most elegant solution. Putting him in San Francisco solves various problems. It is a more natural place for him to be, but still close enough that he could potentially play an important role that could see him as Prince should the Camarilla succeed. Assuming the PCs visit the Vampire Club at some point, they could very well run into him there. He might even be a semi-official liaison to visiting anarchs (or any Kindred in general temporarily visiting the Vampire Club) so the local Kindred can keep a watch on them. He doesn't run the place like Melmoth or Cainen, but he's a club regular so he's a fixture for any regular or frequent visitors.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m glad you like the idea - and as I noted when you suggested the idea on one of the other Free States threads, your idea of LaCroix and Fortier putting their heads together (Especially in a context where the Free States are falling down, if not yet crumbling) since the tacit support of the most influential Ventrue in LA (and possibly in all the Free States) would be a key precondition for LaCroix\u2019s abortive reign as LA\u2019s second Prince - at least to the extent that he would require some sort of nonaggression agreement and for local Ventrue to be encouraged to support (or at least to not oppose him).<br /> <br /> I still doubt that Fortier would go so far as to tie himself directly to LaCroix with a publicly-proclaimed kinship (Whether fictive or actual), at least not until he had proof that LaCroix could do the job (and given there\u2019s ample evidence that the new Prince was mostly in over his head, possibly even completely out of his element, it\u2019s easy to buy that Fortier would prefer to lie low and let events play out, keeping his own interests well out of the firing line).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, LaCroix sharing a Christian name with Don Sebastian is exactly the sort of ominous parallel that would make a seasoned World of Darkness resident extremely nervous about backing this particular \u2018Parachute Prince\u2019.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T10:30:48-07:00","id":1550451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550399#post1550399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm now imagining a weird and wild plot by Christopher the 5th Generation Toreador who is the guy behind Aaron spelling (and sire of Isaac from Bloodlines). Christopher developed yet another one of his &quot;crushes&quot; on Vannevar Thomas and created the Kindred: The Embraced equivalent, Revenant: The Creation, or whatever, and it was something that included a huge number of barely concealed parodies of the main cast.<br /> <br /> Julian Luna/Marcus Sun: The Vannevar Thomas pastiche that is the good hearted Prince who does way more of the dirty work than expected.<br /> <br /> Lilly Langtree; The Prince's Toreador mistress.<br /> <br /> Daedelus: His Sheriff and so on.<br /> <br /> So much so the Camarilla believed this was actually Vannevar's vanity project and removed him from the Princedom for a gross breach of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Hilarious Real Life Matter: White Wolf actually used Vannevar Thomas (even though he'd already been removed as Prince in canon) as part of a marketing stunt for Bloodlines. On the website, Lucita and Vannevar argue about Troika making Bloodlines with the latter saying it'll make any leaks about the Masquerade look ridiculous while Lucita suggests it'll give way too much info to those already in the know.<br /> <br /> I wish it was still online.</div> </div> </div> </div> In all honesty, part of me wonders if it would be even more comical to depict this as the work of Christopher\u2019s oldest surviving Childe trying to persuade Dangerously Underage Vampire Dad to take a closer interest in (and possibly hare off to take a closer look at) San Francisco - or even just trying to engineer a crush on someone more safely distant than Jeremy MacNeil (I\u2019d say \u201cSafely fictional\u201d but the unhappy fate of the chap who played Prince Luna in KINDRED: THE EMBRACED is a matter of record and horribly easy to imagine as a World of Darkness plot point).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, for the record, I tend to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> that the Camarilla can\u2019t afford to make a consistent policy of eliminating excessively-successful Princes for the sake of replacing them with loyal mediocrities, but I can certainly imagine past incarnations of the Inner Circle that would apply this approach when it came to pruning out Princes with a few too many question marks hanging over their Loyalties/Objectives/Family Connections (Probably during periods when the Camarilla is doing sufficiently well that concerns about \u2018Tall Poppy Syndrome\u2019 outweigh the need for independent leadership - or in situations where the Camarilla wishes to keep a powerful and independent Kindred from becoming still more so*).<br /> <br /> I admit that my mental image of the Camarilla is more pragmatic and less systematic than the one suggested by the Conspiracy Theory suggested above - although I absolutely agree that there are elements of the Camarilla leadership who would apply this attitude, if only they could.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I\u2019ve previously used the term \u2018parachute Prince\u2019 and by this I mean a Camarilla stalwart dropped in to take charge of a city where either the political situation is too fragmented by old grudges for one of the local elders to take charge or the city itself is too rich a fief for an old, established Kindred to be entirely trusted with power over it - I doubt the Inner Circle enjoy the idea of another Marcus Vitel or Mithras getting hold of a World Capital, for example.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible that the Inner Circle might send in a Kindred loyal, but less than a heavyweight to assume authority because there\u2019s either a serious risk not worth hazarding a more valuable agent on (or because said agent has ticked off somebody who lacks the power to squash them, but has the influence to pull off a \u2018Uriah gambit\u2019). <br /> <br /> Hence the likes of Sebastian LaCroix: trusted enough to be used, but not popular (or valuable) enough to avoid being misused (I sometimes wonder if the Prince of Rome who vanished at some point circa the Second Anarch Revolt might have been somewhat similar - given the Ancient Grudges and vested interest in Roma it would make sense for the Inner Circle to seek out a compromise candidate \u2026 and possibly an expendable one \u2026 when seeking to appoint the first Full Time Prince of Rome seen in many a century).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T10:56:38-07:00","id":1550455,"title":"","content":"My home Los Angeles game got into the politics of BLOODLINES a bit more than the actual game did (since the Fledgling or &quot;Los Angeles Ripper&quot; as they became known was not privy to these sort of things).<br /> <br /> Basically, poor Sebastian La Croix was subject to a Genghis Gambit from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GenghisGambit\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p.../GenghisGambit</a><br /> <br /> The Anarch Free States were exhausted from fighting their initial war against Kuei Jin and no longer able to keep the Camarilla from asserting praxis in the area. However, whatever Prince was installed had no real chance of asserting true control over the area regardless of how exhausted the Anarchs or Kuei Jin were (and neither was GONE).<br /> <br /> Sebastian La Croix despite being one of Napoleon's calavryman was an Elder who commanded almost no respect or loyalty among the Ventrue. He acts like a preening pompous fool because, well, he is, but he's also under tremendous stress because he KNOWS he's been sent to this prestigious assignment with the full expectation he's going to die.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla's plan, which only Strauss really knows the full parts of, is that they hope Sebastian will do the dirty work enough of killing the Anarchs and Cathayans enough that they will collapse but also being such an annoyance that eventually someone will polish him off. This will end with the Camarilla making a treaty with the survivors and putting their real candidate in charge that will look good by comparison to dear old Sebastian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I want to handle the eastern Kindred. I never really liked it as a setting element because even though China was not well known to Europe, there was lots of contact with India and the Middle East which was also part of the Camarilla. The idea that such Kindred were unknown and mysterious never made sense to me. However, it is part of the original lore so I'll probably go with it. I won't be using Kindred of the East though. I'll use original Gaki and Bushi plus actual folklore and probably handwave a lot of powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>DARK PRINCE had a very interesting idea even way back in 1992, which was the fact that the Kindred of the East were still vampires but they had no relationship to the myth of Caine and had their own organization as well as hierarchy. In my home game, the Eastern Kindred are called the Jade Court (dresden files) and consisted of Cappadocians, Tzimisce, Salubri, and Lasombra (Four being a unlucky number). They go by different names, though, and have slightly different pwers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-28-2025, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T00:13:08-07:00","id":1550474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550455#post1550455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DARK PRINCE had a very interesting idea even way back in 1992, which was the fact that the Kindred of the East were still vampires but they had no relationship to the myth of Caine and had their own organization as well as hierarchy. In my home game, the Eastern Kindred are called the Jade Court (dresden files) and consisted of Cappadocians, Tzimisce, Salubri, and Lasombra (Four being a unlucky number). They go by different names, though, and have slightly different pwers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm perfectly fine with &quot;oriental&quot; vampires referencing their own mythology in terms of the origin of vampires. The Chinese have their own flood myth, and it's not hard to find a correspondence to Cain. I'd probably use Chiyou as the mythological figure associated with vampirism. I probably won't use any of the known 13 clans though to represent the &quot;Eastern Kindred&quot;, but use the Gaki and Bushi examples as inspiration for what the other &quot;clans&quot; would be.<br /> <br /> Limiting them to four would be good though as you noted. Four is unlucky because it is a homonym for death in many east Asian languages.<br /> <br /> The Dresden Files do have a compelling mythology of their own with their various vampire courts. I have utilized those concepts in my Werewolf chronicles to create specific kinds of fomori that correspond to other courts in my chronicle. So having a Jade Court (using whatever name) to represent the Eastern Kindred is not a problem for me. It is something I could see the Inner Circle acknowledging as they try to fit &quot;vampires&quot; who don't &quot;belong&quot; to the Cainite mythology they use.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T18:59:02-07:00","id":1550871,"title":"","content":"As I perform archaeology on old sourcebooks, I find things I'd completely forgotten about. The Ventrue Clanbook 1e has a &quot;distinguished Ventrue&quot; named Stephan Workman. He's a young Ventrue involved in the computer industry who is obviously an analogue of Steve Jobs (the relationship between their names is self-evident). This poor sap isn't even mention in the revised clanbook, and doesn't even have his own page on the White Wolf Wiki despite unknown Kindred, whose only mention is on single V:TES cards, getting their own pages that just repeat what clan they are as shown on their card. One reason might be there is mention of various crossover elements like the Virtual Adepts and Glass Walkers, as well as an attack on him by Eastern Kindred by what is obvious a penanggalan. Revised would have its own very distinct opinions on crossover elements and how the Kindred of the East should be presented.<br /> <br /> However, for our purposes on this thread, this is a great character. Steve Jobs as a Ventrue vampire in San Jose is an interesting element. He's obviously not an anarch, but must somehow be tolerated by them. Possibly because a lot of older Ventrue hate him for disrupting their influence over older technology companies. A major difference is that Stephan Workman is probably not known by the general public, unlike Steve Jobs. He'd be more like an almost anonymous venture capitalist who supports and funds entrepreneurs like Steve Jobs. I imagine many anarchs simply enjoy him annoying older, more established Ventrue without realizing he's going to become king of Silicon Valley and an incredibly important member of clan Ventrue's global directorate. He's interesting flavor in early nineties California. He'd be the new Horatio Ballard in 2025 controlling vast swaths of the global economy.<br /> <br /> As a Ventrue in San Jose, his sire is most likely a Ventrue from San Francisco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T11:05:31-07:00","id":1550883,"title":"","content":"If he\u2019s not a Childe of Vannevar Thomas himself, he\u2019s<br /> almost certainly a \u2018Grand Childe\u2019 of San Francisco\u2019s Prince - or if he\u2019s not, then we may have an excellent reason for the Anarchs allowing him to go about his business unmolested (Besides the beating heart of the Free States being more interested in politics, philosophy and revolutionary violence than doing Big Business or observing same), especially if the relatively young Workman serves as a low-key insurgent in Thomas\u2019 fief (An outrageously rich Ventrue spreading the wealth in all the right places - or declining to do so - could be a key precondition for the series of events that saw Prince Vannevar Thomas ousted from San Francisco).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible that Workman is instead a Childe of the Ventrue primogen in San Francisco, though it would be deeply odd for that individual to NOT be a Childe of San Francisco\u2019s Ventrue prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T20:41:20-07:00","id":1550897,"title":"","content":"Based on the description of Stephan Workman there is a good chance he's not related to Prince Vannevar at all. He was originally a ghoul who worked on electrical devices and embraced later when his sire found he was good at managing companies. This isn't Steve Jobs head of Apple, this is Steve Jobs building computers in his garage. That he became this important Ventrue in Silicon Valley was totally unexpected. Being related to the Prince would increase the chance of difficulties with the anarchs so I'll assume he isn't.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, while Vannevar is skilled in politics like Lodin and works to keep the Primogen divided so they don't unite against him, he doesn't have a particularly large brood like Lodin nor is he trying to dominate the city. The Ventrue Primogen, Nickolai, is certainly not related to Vannevar. He's a recent neonate from Russia who arrived in San Francisco after the Great Fire.<br /> <br /> Of course, I am not beholden to canon and am quick to change anything I do not like. But simply because of the sheer size of the Free States and trying to evaluate nearby domains as to how they might affect things, I am prone to stealing as much from canon as I like just to lessen my workload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T09:34:38-07:00","id":1550958,"title":"","content":"Making Stephan Workman (It amuses me to imagine that he pronounces the name \u2018Stefan\u2019 to give himself a little Old World Vampire dignity) the Childe of Nikolai would be an excellent way to give the latter some immediate relevancy - especially if we give Nikolai something of a \u2018Russian Nikolai Tesla\u2019 sort of aura and a very technocratic sort of focus (Small \u2018t\u2019, obviously).<br /> <br /> If he had to get out of Russia in AD 1906, it\u2019s possible he\u2019s a pre-Bolshevik Revolutionary who made the Motherland just a bit too hot to hold him and has been trying to get a little credit from Soviet Russia ever since (Despite originally being attached to some rival revolutionary.<br /> <br /> In fact one could depict him as somebody who tired of Revolutionary politics and decided to focus on Revolutionary technology instead - which might lend itself to an interesting dynamic with the Anarchs, whilst explaining why he prefer the Bay Area to the Free States proper.<br /> <br /> Heck, his playing both sides against the middle would definitely lend itself to an interesting dynamic with Prince Vannevar Thomas and the Anarch higher-ups (Especially if he\u2019s genuinely impartial, rather than purely cynical).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T17:13:12-07:00","id":1550978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1550958#post1550958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he had to get out of Russia in AD 1906, it\u2019s possible he\u2019s a pre-Bolshevik Revolutionary who made the Motherland just a bit too hot to hold him and has been trying to get a little credit from Soviet Russia ever since (Despite originally being attached to some rival revolutionary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nickolai was a Russian aristocrat and former advisor to Nicholas II. Unknown when he was embraced, but it had to have been fairly recent. Also unknown are the exact reasons he left, but presumably he ran afoul of what would become the Brujah Council and decided to get out. Exact arrival in San Francisco would be sometime between 1906-1916. That he's in SF and not elsewhere indicates he likely left while WWI was already going on. If his backstory became important, I'd probably have him associated with Pyotr Stolypin when he was a mortal.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T18:31:22-07:00","id":1551031,"title":"","content":"I learn something new everyday. I found another mention of San Jose. It's something that seems to contradict prior established canon, but I expect that now. The Revised era's setting pretty much is its own Earth-Two to the Earth-One of the 1//2e era.<br /> <br /> In the sourcebook Havens of the Damned, there's actually an entry on the Winchester Mystery House. It is inhabited by the secret &quot;architect&quot; of the house, the Malkavian Jonathon Smith. Very creative name there. Also creative is that his sire was the Malkavian Ivo Shandor who in a mad fit convinced Smith to diablerize him so Smith now hears Ivo's voice telling him what to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a4TPo8eYEs0\" data-code=\"a4TPo8eYEs0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/a4TPo8eYEs0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm all in favor of people's home chronicles using whatever they want. I think this would be hilarious and nice homage in someone's chronicle. But in an officially published sourcebook this kind of direct reference to another media should not be done. Isn't that why all the characters from Upton Sinclair's The Jungle were killed off in Under a Blood Red Moon?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Smith followed Winchester to her new home in San Jose, hid in her house, and by gaslighting her during seances, indirectly controlled how the house would be built. Smith may (or may not) have combined Dementation and some blood ritual to be able to mentally control the layout of the house in some kind of non-euclidean nightmare that may or may not lead to extradimensional travel. Or that may just be his delusion. Sara Winchester herself now haunts the house herself since Smith was the one who killed her by drinking her blood.<br /> <br /> The LABN sourcebook obviously does not mention this, but does mention in its San Jose entry. It says several Kindred have tried claiming it as a haven, but that none have survived their first night. Obviously, it is possible to reconcile these two versions by saying that it is Smith who is somehow destroying any new Kindred who intrude.<br /> <br /> In the Changeling game, the Winchester Mystery House is also a powerful source of Glamour with hundreds of chimerical creatures and objects. No changelings live here because there's too many dangerous creatures, but some do visit to harvest glamour and screw around with things. Again, this does not technically contradict the haven in Havens of the Damned, but I'm pretty sure the author of the Havens entry ignored everything previously mentioned.<br /> <br /> Will I use this in my chronicle? Probably not directly, but I might use the general idea of some powerful Malkavian dwelling within the house be responsible for a lot of odd things in San Jose. Maybe his occasional activities outside the house creates enough uncertainty and confusion that it keeps the anarchs unbalanced and uncertain how to proceed. So they take a live and let live approach to things. I'm more inclined the make house itself some kind of haunt with a circle of wraiths there because I think Wraith works better with Vampire than Changeling. Maybe they can make use of this particular Malkavian so they help him out if other Kindred intrude in it. Maybe the wraiths here are skilled in classic haunting Arcanoi like Pandemonium, but also the forbidden Arcanoi like Flux and possibly Intimation and Mnemosynis. It would make them capable defenders that could really confuse any intruders exploring the house. Also being the home of a crazy vampire with mental powers might make it less suspicious to the Hierarchy if they hear of &quot;hauntings&quot; there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T14:04:48-07:00","id":1551051,"title":"","content":"It amuses me to imagine that \u2018Jonathan Smith\u2019 is this Malkavian\u2019s born name and that he\u2019s the sort of Malkavian who speaks in a painfully-normal drone that makes him sound like a less than enthusiastic tour guide (Whilst dressed in clothes that were impeccably-normal at some point during the construction of the Winchester House - further strengthening the impression of a tour guide dangerous only through being deathly dull) unless somebody with a sufficiently strong attention span notes that (amongst other Red Flags) he\u2019s referring to \u2018Ivo Shandor\u2019 as a person who actually exists and at points acts as though he\u2019s actually speaking to the man in person, without a walkie talkie or the impression that somebody else has actually entered the room.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am strongly implying that Mr Smith\u2019s sense of reality is sufficiently weak that his reaction to watching GHOSTBUSTERS was to hear the name \u2018Ivo Shandor\u2019, think \u201cOh that sounds like Vampire Dad\u201d and start using that name in preference to his Sire\u2019s actual name (Which makes it much, much harder to work out just where the heck this guy is coming from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T13:55:36-07:00","id":1551081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551051#post1551051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I am strongly implying that Mr Smith\u2019s sense of reality is sufficiently weak that his reaction to watching GHOSTBUSTERS was to hear the name \u2018Ivo Shandor\u2019, think \u201cOh that sounds like Vampire Dad\u201d and start using that name in preference to his Sire\u2019s actual name (Which makes it much, much harder to work out just where the heck this guy is coming from).</div> </div> </div> </div>This would probably be the only reason I would ever include &quot;Ivo Shandor&quot; as part of this character's backstory. This Malkavian actually think Ghostbusters (and perhaps some other movies) is real and incorporates elements of that movie into his life as part of his delusion. Other characters may or may not pick up on a reference to &quot;Ivo Shandor&quot;, but they probably will to references to Venkman, Stantz, Spengler, or Wilson. Or Gozer worshippers in general.<br /> <br /> Maybe the character is some kind of expert on ghosts, but he thinks a lot of ghost movies he's seen are in fact real. Ghostbusters is one of them, but so is Beetlejuice, Ghost, Candyman, Poltergeist, the Shining, and many others. Maybe his derangement does in fact allows him to see ghosts. But can anyone trusts what he says about them at any one time?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T14:18:07-07:00","id":1551087,"title":"","content":"When writing any Malkavian mixing genuine insight with <i>just</i> enough crazy to make PCs consider what the individual Malkavian say very, very carefully is surely the way to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> On an equally serious note, having just worked out that the Bay Area of the early AD 1990s could support roughly 60-90 vampires (The former based on standard Camarilla ratio, the latter on an \u2018Anarch ratio\u2019 about halfway between the Camarilla and the Sabbat), then estimating that San Francisco proper could support about 7 of those vampires (By strict Camarilla ratio) and noting that there are said to be 10 Anarchs in San Jose, it occurs to me that this leaves between 40-70 vampires in locations to be determined.<br /> <br /> Now I tend to assume that local Kindred numbers are on the lower end (Since Werewolves are unusually at home in the Bay Area cities, according to one source and since the region appears to be something of \u2018demilitarised zone\u2019 between Anarchs &amp; Ivory Tower), but this still leaves roughly 40 vampires to play with.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it might be interesting to depict a fairly substantial between-the-lines population playing Camarilla and Anarch by turns for their own advantage (In the absence of a powerful Baron and in the presence of a Camarilla prince who has to step carefully wjen passing beyond the bounds of the Bay City proper, Palatine or no).<br /> <br /> It IS possible that San Francisco is somewhat overpopulated by Camarilla standards, but it might be more interesting to show San Fran as more of a fallback position than a permanent residence for many Camarilla members in the Bay Area.<br /> <br /> Anyway, might I please ask your thoughts on the matter <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T17:08:27-07:00","id":1551090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551087#post1551087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an equally serious note, having just worked out that the Bay Area of the early AD 1990s could support roughly 60-90 vampires (The former based on standard Camarilla ratio, the latter on an \u2018Anarch ratio\u2019 about halfway between the Camarilla and the Sabbat), then estimating that San Francisco proper could support about 7 of those vampires (By strict Camarilla ratio) and noting that there are said to be 10 Anarchs in San Jose, it occurs to me that this leaves between 40-70 vampires in locations to be determined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonical vampire populations are based on the mortal population of the metropolitan area, not the city itself. I think the idea is that even though people in the suburbs don't live in the city (and the suburbs are considered to be &quot;barrens&quot; where hunting is difficult because of lack of nightlight, low crime, and lack of anonymity), the people there are constantly commuting to and from the city making themselves available. Like all game conventions, it's just meant as a convenient way to quickly calculate an &quot;appropriate&quot; amount of vampires. While it has no basis in reality, I accept it in my games.<br /> <br /> The Bay Area is obviously quite large geographically and divided into several distinct urban zones. I would use three, meaning there are three separate domains. However, it's entirely possible it is (or could be) one domain that is useful to think of consisting of three parts. Roughly speaking that is San Francisco area itself, the East Bay around Oakland, and the South Bay around San Jose<br /> <br /> San Francisco metro area itself likely encompasses San Francisco and San Mateo counties for a combined population of around 1.5 million in 1990. So probably around 15-20 vampires.<br /> <br /> Oakland metro area probably consists of Contra Costa and Alameda counties for a combined population of around 2.0 million in 1990. While San Francisco itself is the larger city, this is where most of the population is at. Probably another 20 vampires. I'll admit I did not know how large the East Bay counties were until I just did research right now.<br /> <br /> Then there is the San Jose metro area in Santa Clara county which is another 1.7 million in 1990. LABN only shows San Jose's actual population of 782k at the time, and thus estimates 10 vampires here. If we use the county's population and the great ratio of anarch vampires, 17-25 vampires.<br /> <br /> That is over five million people all together. Maybe 52-65 vampires total. The SF metro area turns out to be the smallest one of the three, but definitely the oldest with the most established vampires and a thriving tourist industry.<br /> <br /> The North Bay comprises four counties - Marin, Sonoma, Napa, and Solano counties. Their combined population is around 1.1 million in 1990, but that is spread out over a fairly large area. Most of it rural. There is probably very little Kindred activity in Marin and Sonoma because of the presence of a Garou caern. I would place this in a separate category and remove it from normal Kindred population except for some Gangrel and occasional loner vampire keeping low in wine country.<br /> <br /> Back in 1945, urban sprawl was low enough that Vannevar Thomas was probably the only real prince. Oakland would have had vampires, but would either have been considered part of Vannevar's domain, or its prince would probably be in a defacto or even dejure subordinate to Vannevar. San Jose would not even be considered as its own entity in terms of vampires.<br /> <br /> San Jose probably had the presence of anarchs to make it a contested territory, but that would probably not have been enough to be its own &quot;barony&quot; until the boom years of Silicon Valley in the seventies. At that point the presence of anarchs likely made it be considered its own &quot;domain&quot; separate from Vannevar's rule in San Francisco itself.<br /> <br /> The decision to make San Francisco some kind of separate, independent &quot;palatinate&quot; would have made Oakland and the East Bay an important Camarilla domain. It's probably there that any archons &quot;officially&quot; reside, and the Camarilla would have supported (and possibly controlled) any Prince of the East Bay. The urban growth of the East Bay might even have been a plan by the Camarilla to cement its power in the area.<br /> <br /> The East Bay is essentially ignored by LABN probably because nobody thought Oakland and its environs was important enough to mention. Based on the hard to read map of California there, it appears Oakland is supposed to be part of the Free States. However, there is no mention of an Oakland barony. Oakland also doesn't seem to be mentioned in the Anarch Cookbook either. We could see a theoretical &quot;three way&quot; contest between the anarchs in the South Bay, the palatinate in SF proper, and the Camarilla in the East Bay. Of the three, the Camarilla's control of the East Bay would mean they have the slightly larger population between the three. <br /> <br /> That might also be another reason the anarchs don't move on SF. They could be caught in a pincer move between Vannevar and the Camarilla if they attack one. Instead, Vannevar plays up his independence and the possible &quot;common enemy&quot; he and the anarchs have. SF and the East Bay could play a good cop/bad cop thing between them to keep the local anarchs in control. Indeed, since the palatinate likely only exists because of the anarch threat, a complete victory over the Free States would soon see another Conclave that revokes the Treaty. Therefore, Vannevar may even help the anarchs in some capacity some of the time, earning some grudging respect and showcasing how important it is that SF keeps its status quo.<br /> <br /> It might be interesting to have the anarch NPCs mention <i>Oakland</i> as the big Camarilla threat then rather than San Francisco. That should surprise players. And as San Jose grows in population and economic power (today it is the largest city in the Bay Area and third largest in the state), simply keeping it anarch would be a sufficient challenge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T13:09:14-07:00","id":1551348,"title":"","content":"I have to say, the Bay Area being in the middle of a constant (or at least consistent) game of Musical Chairs - with the Garou keeping a hungry eye on the region for good measure and at least some Changeling presence to boot - must keep things interesting (Especially in the \u2018debatable lands\u2019).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T00:43:43-07:00","id":1551362,"title":"","content":"I've arbitrarily decided that the Prince of the East Bay is Maxwell from Chicago By Night, 2e. I'm being very lazy at the moment, and he's an available &quot;prince&quot; for this time period. For canon purists, consider him a different character with the same name and general back story. <br /> <br /> As a Brujah from Mexico who is either a mulatto or pardo, he fits the California venue and would prove an effective foil for the anarchs. A Brujah prince of Oakland would have a different effect on many anarchs than a prince from a different clan. Remove any existing prince in 1946-1948 and slip in an elder Brujah instead. It could have happened at the same conclave that established the palatinate.<br /> <br /> I assume &quot;Maxwell&quot; is simply the Americanized version of his real name which is probably Maximiliano.<br /> <br /> The entire issue or consideration of Oakland and the East Bay is not something I would likely have established on my own so this is something I owe to this board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-08T16:41:53-07:00","id":1551533,"title":"","content":"So based on the above, I'm using this for the population of vampires in San Francisco Bay circa 1992:<br /> <br /> San Francisco itself is around twenty vampires. A bit higher than the metro area suggests because SF is a tourist hotspot with lots of intransigents passing through. East Bay is also twenty vampires.<br /> <br /> I'm also putting San Jose as twenty as well. Ten anarchs to use the figure in LABN plus another ten vampires loosely affiliated with the Camarilla or &quot;neutral&quot;. That allows for vampires like the Ventrue Stephan Workman. The anarchs and non-anarchs more or less tolerate each other. No one is really in charge, and each side respects the other's turf. Nobody wants to be responsible for initiating a conflict that might suck in SF, Oakland, or LA. San Jose and Santa Clara County is booming at this time with large increases in population so nobody is hurting for feeding territory.<br /> <br /> The VtM fiction stories set in San Francisco makes the standard assumption of seven primogen, each representing one of the clans of the Inner Circle. While popular, I have never liked this conceit. Chicago By Night did not follow this. Neither the Malkavians or Ventrue had a member on the primogen council, and the Brujah had two (possibly three at one time) members. IMO, the primogen are simply the most powerful individual vampires in a domain who seek to wield influence collectively. They aren't some official clan representatives. There's no problem for a chronicle to have one from each clan, but it isn't some Camarilla rule.<br /> <br /> In regards to San Francisco, having seven primogen means the primogen alone are one third to one half the entire vampire population of the city. That seems far too high for me. I don't think domains should be that top heavy. You need a lot more lower status and neonate vampires than high status elders. It's likely Keith Herbert, the author of Dark Prince, never bothered to consider what the population of San Francisco should be when he populated his domain, or perhaps he simply considered the domain to be the entire San Francisco Bay area (a defensible choice, but not one I am using here). So I am arbitrarily splitting the canonical SF primogen between SF and Oakland. So who to keep and who to remove?<br /> <br /> The canonical members (at the time of the first novel, Dark Prince):<ul><li>Tomaine (Brujah Primogen)</li> <li>Alicia McGreb (Gangrel Primogen)</li> <li>Bloody Mary (Malkavian Primogen)</li> <li>The Dowager (Nosferatu Primogen)</li> <li>Allanyan Serata (Toreador Primogen)</li> <li>Honerius (Tremere Primogen)</li> <li>Nickolai (Ventrue Primogen)</li> </ul>Who to keep in San Francisco? The Dowager is strongly associated with Chinatown so she has to stay. Likewise there is a strong Toreador influence in the city. Since Sebastian Melmoth is non-political, I'm keeping Allanyan Serata. Honerius is involved in several high stakes plots in canon, so I'll keep him there as well. I am also keeping Nickolai as a character although whether he's actually a primogen I'll decide later. Those four plus the Prince, Sebastian Melmoth, and Tex R. Cainen means there's still only 8-12 more vampires total. Not a whole lot if you're hoping to include vampires from the other clans and multiple factions. This is basically a domain of Ventrue, Nosferatu, and Toreador plus one Tremere chantry. Very few characters of anyone else. Very much a &quot;high clans&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> That means I'm moving Tomaine, Alicia McGreb, and Bloody Mary over to the East Bay. They all seem to have the least personality and least overt ties to iconic San Francisco elements so moving them to Oakland isn't much of a loss. Some of them may have even dwelled in San Francisco at some point, perhaps only moving to the East Bay later. The East Bay will be a stronghold of the other Camarilla clans - Brujah, Gangrel, and Malkavian. Not exclusively, but these three clans dominate.<br /> when needed as well any other anarch coterie. It's not like you need to live there to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T08:44:39-07:00","id":1551537,"title":"","content":"Something to be considered is the nature of the Palatine Treaty - if I remember correctly then it gives uncommon (possibly unique) status and powers to the Prince of San Francisco <i>and</i> to his Primogen, so it\u2019s far from impossible that this would be a potent incentive for potent elders to become involved with San Francisco.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the fact \u2018Frisco is a lonely Camarilla enclave in the Free States and a fallback position for those ousted during the Second Anarch Revolt: it\u2019s quite plausible that even without the Palatine Treaty more than one elder would linger in the Bay Area in the same way that Jacobite Exiles clustered within spitting distance of Great Britain after the \u2018Glorious Revolution\u2019 (In the hopes of reclaiming further haunts or at least settling a few old grudges).<br /> <br /> Still, I do love the plot hooks suggested by a political situation where the question of whether Prince Vannevar Thomas is Prince of San Francisco only or Prince of San Francisco Bay remains an open one \u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T08:51:12-07:00","id":1551538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551362#post1551362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've arbitrarily decided that the Prince of the East Bay is Maxwell from Chicago By Night, 2e. I'm being very lazy at the moment, and he's an available &quot;prince&quot; for this time period. For canon purists, consider him a different character with the same name and general back story.<br /> <br /> As a Brujah from Mexico who is either a mulatto or pardo, he fits the California venue and would prove an effective foil for the anarchs. A Brujah prince of Oakland would have a different effect on many anarchs than a prince from a different clan. Remove any existing prince in 1946-1948 and slip in an elder Brujah instead. It could have happened at the same conclave that established the palatinate.<br /> <br /> I assume &quot;Maxwell&quot; is simply the Americanized version of his real name which is probably Maximiliano.<br /> <br /> The entire issue or consideration of Oakland and the East Bay is not something I would likely have established on my own so this is something I owe to this board.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you want to be extremely cheeky, you could borrow the name \u2018Julian Luna\u2019 from KINDRED: THE EMBRACED and leave it ambiguous as to whether this is the character\u2019s actual name or an alter ego they\u2019ve adopted as a way to cock a snook at Prince Vannevar Thomas - at least in their \u2018official proclamations\u2019.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, it\u2019s interesting to wonder whether \u2018Maxwell 2.0\u2019/Julian Luna might be a broodmate or Childe of Maxwell himself - we know that the latter is extremely happy to embrace and then send out his new vampire into the world, seeking whatever might be useful to Vampire Dad, so why not aim for California?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T12:31:56-07:00","id":1551566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551537#post1551537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to be considered is the nature of the Palatine Treaty - if I remember correctly then it gives uncommon (possibly unique) status and powers to the Prince of San Francisco <i>and</i> to his Primogen, so it\u2019s far from impossible that this would be a potent incentive for potent elders to become involved with San Francisco.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not been able to find much information on the unique status of San Francisco. The Palatine Treaty was referenced in both A World of Darkness 1e and Anarch Cookbook, but we're not given many details. We need to interpret a lot. The Palatine Council is mentioned, but nothing else is known about it. I just assume it's just a normal primogen council, but renamed to denote the domain's status.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that essentially San Francisco is an &quot;independent&quot; domain much like Siegfried's rule in Vancouver, but acknowledged by the Camarilla as part of the treaty in the 1946 Conclave (and thus potentially revoked by another conclave). It has to be allied to the Camarilla in some sense and probably bound to enforce the Six Traditions. But unlike other princes who are constantly worried about the Justicars and archons poking around in their business, Vannevar Thomas rules alone (although with the usual caveats of the primogen influencing him in some capacity). For now at least.<br /> <br /> Declaring cities as &quot;free&quot; is not unique. Siegfried declared himself as Prince of Vancouver &quot;in the mid-forties,&quot; but rules without consent of the Camarilla. Prince Sarasine declared Sydney (Australia) as a free city in the mid-fifties also without consent of the Camarilla. Whether or not intended by the writers, it is hard not to imagine this was done in imitation of the Palatine of San Francisco except in their case it was not done under the legitimacy of a conclave. Both domains were remote in terms of the traditional power centers of the Camarilla, and such declarations would have been made at a time when both Princes believed the Camarilla would not make much effort to overthrow them for whatever reasons. I'm sure the Justicars intend at some point to reassert the Inner Circle's authority in both domains. It's likely in Petrodon's case that selecting Seattle as his base of operations was to keep eyes on both the Free States and Vancouver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T04:40:41-07:00","id":1551654,"title":"","content":"If your theories about Vancouver and Sydney are correct, then it\u2019s small wonder that an element within the Camarilla would be willing (and possibly working) to exile Prince Vannevar Thomas from his city just as soon as it can safely be done (I.E. after the collapse of the Free States).<br /> <br /> One can only wonder if this is known to Kindred on the ground in the Bay Area and what sort of intrigue, factional bickering or outright faction-fighting it might produce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T14:12:28-07:00","id":1551660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551654#post1551654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If your theories about Vancouver and Sydney are correct, then it\u2019s small wonder that an element within the Camarilla would be willing (and possibly working) to exile Prince Vannevar Thomas from his city just as soon as it can safely be done (I.E. after the collapse of the Free States).<br /> <br /> One can only wonder if this is known to Kindred on the ground in the Bay Area and what sort of intrigue, factional bickering or outright faction-fighting it might produce.</div> </div> </div> </div>San Francisco's status as a &quot;Palatine&quot; only makes sense given the threat of the Anarch Free States. If the Free States are ever eliminated, then that status won't last long afterwards. Petrodon (or another Justicar) calls a conclave, pulls in as much support as he can, and revokes the Palatine Treaty. What that means for Vannevar really depends on his personal relationships with other Kindred and the exact circumstances of the original treaty. If it was an attempt to protect San Francisco from an anarch conquest by both Vannevar and the Justicar, Vannevar could very well survive as Prince even if resigned to interference in the future. If it was more of Vannevar extracting concessions from the Justicar desperate to hold off the anarchs, the Camarilla will take revenge.<br /> <br /> In either case, Vannevar likely has reasons to tactically cooperate with the Anarch Free States as his new independence depends on their ongoing survival. They have a common &quot;enemy&quot;. Vannevar might share certain information with the anarchs through some intermediary at the Vampire Club (perhaps Sebastian La Croix?) It makes San Francisco (and the Vampire Club) much more like the movie Casablanca described in A World of Darkness, and much less like the enemy Camarilla bastion described in LABN. Since I like the idea of utilizing the Vampire Club as a setting element, I lean more towards A World of Darkness. Creating an Oakland/East Bay domain that is Camarilla loyal still allows me to present a Camarilla threat on the northern border of the Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T12:46:27-07:00","id":1551771,"title":"","content":"Prince Vannevar Thomas being unwary enough to trust his communications with the Anarch Free States to Sebastian LaCroix would be an excellent explanation for how both of them ended up ex-Princes in the published timeline (One more fatally than the other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T13:02:18-07:00","id":1551844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551538#post1551538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to be extremely cheeky, you could borrow the name \u2018Julian Luna\u2019 from KINDRED: THE EMBRACED and leave it ambiguous as to whether this is the character\u2019s actual name or an alter ego they\u2019ve adopted as a way to cock a snook at Prince Vannevar Thomas - at least in their \u2018official proclamations\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>Named canon characters actually take up much of the numbers that San Francisco &quot;should' have based on the classic 1:100k ratio. It's fairly obvious Keith Herbert and others simply didn't bother to consider this when writing their stories. (It's possible they were using the entire Bay Area population although I find this unlikely since stories usually don't reference anything in the East Bay.) Bit of a failure at world building there. So there isn't much room for more characters in SF proper unless one removes some canon characters.<br /> <br /> However, the domain at the East Bay/Oakland is completely undefined. Even putting in &quot;Maxwell&quot; there and moving over some of the canon SF primogen to there still leaves well over a dozen characters. Stealing some of the characters (or at least their concepts, possibly with some names named and biographical details changed) from K:TE for the East Bay would help that along. May need to change some of the clans and relationships around.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of undefined vampires in San Jose. I think besides Stephen Workman in San Jose, there may not be any other known canon characters there. I'm keeping Ventrue, Toreador, and Tremere mostly in SF, and putting Brujah, Gangrel, and Malkavian mostly to East Bay. So K:TE characters that are Ventrue and Toreador that can't fit in overpopulated SF and shouldn't be in the East Bay may just end up in San Jose. Could be the place for a Ventrue named Julian Luna there (and Toreador named Lillie Langtry). Luna might have ambitions to be Prince of San Jose/South Bay one day (it would explain his large brood - while not a Prince who can sire at will, as someone in an Anarch controlled area, he can sire as much as any anarch). Luna would be a good antagonist for my PCs. Fighting or even destroying him won't cause the same kind of repercussions as if the PCs went against him the Prince of San Francisco or Oakland. It's a fight that can be contained to just San Jose.<br /> <br /> Of course, while geographically distinct from each because of San Francisco Bay, everything is within easy driving distance from each other. Kindred from the West Bay, East Bay, and South Bay probably all run into each other. They show up at the Vampire Club or other Kindred locale, make deals with each other, and so on. It's just that there are three separate power centers that control things in their third of the Bay, and characters have favored feeding places in &quot;their&quot; domain and less favored in other domains.<br /> <br /> The more I think about this, I really like the way the Kindred of San Francisco Bay are developing. It provides a lot of opportunity for my PCs. For those who want to take the fight to the Camarilla, there are several options including a &quot;safe&quot; option for physical violence in San Jose. For those who want more traditional Camarilla salon scenes, there's the Vampire Club in SF which is open to all. If you want subtle intrigue, you have it. If you want a more tyrannical, heavy handed Prince to complain about, there's Prince Maxwell in Oakland.<br /> <br /> I don't intend for the Bay Area to be the primary arena for the game. That remains Los Angeles. However, if players ever want to explore more or develop ties to actual Camarilla characters, it's there to be used. The rather wide expanse of the Free States covering multiple urban areas is a good way to distinguish it from other settings. Things typically take place in one city, and while there's nothing to theoretically stop PCs from residing in Chicago but travelling to Milwaukee, Rockford, Peoria, etc., that's rarely done. Both STs and players tend to hunker down in one metro area. While I could that too in LA, I like the sense that there's wide open freedom for anarchs to travel to nearby domains because the Tradition of Hospitality is not enforced. It means a lot more work for me, but I think my players will appreciate the freedom of such a large sandbox.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T14:10:57-07:00","id":1551866,"title":"","content":"I must admit to letting my imagination wander whither it will - if it ever goes somewhere and comes back with unhelpful souvenirs, please do let me know.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T20:29:58-07:00","id":1551934,"title":"","content":"I have terrible friends. One actually had ancient copies of the Dark Prince and Prince of the City novels from the nineties. So I actually read them to see what details I could pull from the city's NPCs. I read through them very fast and skipped bits so I may have missed some things. Apologies if I make any errors. There are also some continuity discrepancies between the books, but that might be attributed to unreliable narrators. There are two distinct groups of vampires in them that are very peculiar whom I want to discuss.<br /> <br /> The first is known as the Family. It's a group of vampires mainly from China who run most of Chinatown. It's headed by a huge, mysterious vampire in a demonic wooden mask called the Grandfather. The Grandfather's childe is a beautiful female vampire called Kwon, and her childe is a small, very young looking male vampire called Loo. They arrive in San Francisco in 1851 on a ship with all its crew dead (much like the Demeter in Dracula). Kwon ends up embracing an Irish-American crimp named Sullivan to help them navigate the unfamilar Western city of San Francisco. Although Kwon subsequently dies in the backstory, these three vampires of &quot;the Family&quot; have a somewhat important role in the city, and Sullivan serves as the protagonist of Dark Prince.<br /> <br /> The clan of these vampires is never mentioned. I assume it was meant to be some clan of the Kindred of the East when they were still conceived as mechanically part of the VtM line instead of the more Risen like undead of the Kindred of the East sourcebooks (which came out four years after Dark Prince). They are pretty much like any other vampires in the book. So how to translate them? I won't be using the KOTE sourcebook at all for my chronicle. The Family is clearly some traditional clan of Vampire so I am going with that. I still think they should be somewhat unusual and exotic for the traditional Camarilla setting vampires. So I'll be retconning them to be Lasombra anti-tribu vampires from Canton/Guangzhou. Most Chinese immigrants to California at this time came from the Pearl River Delta where Canton is located. In addition, Canton as a port was open to trade with much of India and the Middle East during the Song and early Ming dynasties. Very easy to justify that some Lasombra made his way to that port at some point in the Middle Ages and embraced someone local like the Grandfather. Separated from most vampire politics, these Lasombra would have never experienced the Anarch Revolt or the transformation of the clan into what it would become under the Sabbat. For reasons of their own, the Family decided to come to San Francisco during the Gold Rush, and they have remained ever since.<br /> <br /> I don't really think it makes sense for them to have embraced Sullivan as he would have been better in his role by being a ghoul. So to keep their numbers up to three, I'll keep Kwon surviving. Nobody actually knows that they are in fact &quot;Lasombra&quot;, but have accepted them as being part of the domain. For lieu of any actual clan name, they just call them the Family. It's possible the Tremere (or perhaps some other elders) have figured things out, but if so it hasn't gotten out to the general Kindred population.<br /> <br /> The other peculiar group are three vampires descended from a line of Aztec vampires. The first is Hortator, an Aztec priest who was an advisor to Montezuma. He later becomes Vannevar's chief bodyguard and private counsel. Then there is Hortator's childe, Diego don Delfonso (a Spanish conquistador who came with Cortes). Then there is Delfonso's childe Domingo, a WWII era zoot suit hooligan. Delfonso has the honor of being the first vampire to reside in San Francisco (since 1777 shortly after the Spanish Presidio and Mission were built).<br /> <br /> Obviously Hortator can't be the Aztec priests's mortal name. It's a Latin noun meaning &quot;inciter&quot; or &quot;encourager.&quot; It was also used as the title for the man who beat the drums of the galley slaves in the novel Ben-Hur, but I don't know if that is correct historical usage or something the author, Lew Wallace, made up. It's not clear to me why this character has been given this name, presumably a nickname used for him by some other vampire (Delfonso?) or self-applied once the priest learned Latin. It's also important to note that Hortator - since he was a human priest in service to Montezuma - could not have been a vampire long before he embraced Delfonso.<br /> <br /> These three vampires are all accepted by the local vampires of San Francisco. However, their clan is never mentioned, and in Prince of the City Vannevar even states that &quot;his true bloodline was<br /> obscure, his clan unknown\u200b&quot;. However, much like the Family, they are not treated as Caitiff.<br /> <br /> While as a general rule it's stated that the New World was free of vampires, by the time these books were written it was already canon that some vampires did in fact arrive in the Americas pre-Columbian contact. They also seemed to congregate in Mesoamerica, the first real urban civilization there. Diablerie: Mexico introduced the Wanderer (a Gangrel) and mentioned some other vampires, and the Chaos Factor introduced the Baali Huitzilopochtli. Both masqueraded as local deities. It's not clear if they sired childer, but these would be the best candidates for any line of local vampires that could have sired Hortator. Much later than these books, the revised Clanbook: Followers of Set introduced the Tlacique, a bloodline thought to be from the Setites. Giovanni Clanbook introduced the Pisanob, Aztec necromancers embraced by the Giovanni although I think they're clearly embraced post-Conquest. Still, it's possible Pochtli could have embraced Hortator who simply wandered off. For people who want to adhere as closely to canon as possible, these are your possible picks.<br /> <br /> For me, I'll be mixing some canon together. I'll be keeping the Tlacique, but making them a variant of the Gangrel except that their Protean defaults to the jaguar and not the world because that is the main predator in that region. Their in-clan Disciplines remain the Gangrel in-clan Disciplines, but they do have a heritage of indigenous Nahuallotl blood sorcery. Some of which Hortator knows. These vampires aren't popularly known/suspected to be Gangrel, but some elder vampires think they are most likely some ancient remnant of the Gangrel and thus afford them such acceptance. I'm sure other STs will select something different that works for them.<br /> <br /> I'm going to include these character into my version of San Francisco. They provide some nice local flavor, but more importantly I think they provide another reason why Vannevar's San Franciso was considered to be a hard target for the anarchs. If he has allies among some rather old, mysterious, and fairly unknown type of &quot;Chinese&quot; and &quot;Aztec&quot; vampires, it could give other vampires some pause. A surviving anarch whose coterie was wiped out in San Francisco by weird jaguar vampires and scary Chinese &quot;sorcerers&quot; would have some terrifying stories to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T10:51:41-07:00","id":1551947,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t speak for the rest, but I know enough about classical history to confirm that \u2018hortator\u2019 is the term for a war-galley\u2019s equivalent to the coxswain in a modern competitive rowing team (Though my understanding is that the war galleys of the classical world were more often manned by paid professionals, not slave labour).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming that the \u2018Hortator\u2019 in question had some history at sea (Or at least of \u2018encouraging\u2019 a captive audience) to help explain the name; I also wonder if this might have been an individual who made common cause with the Spanish at some point (Possibly one of the peoples subject to the Aztecs who sided with the Spanish to oust their former lords and<br /> masters, only to acquire a new set).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T10:57:15-07:00","id":1551949,"title":"","content":"Oh, as for Sullivan being taken into the family as a fledgling rather than a ghoul, this might well be a product of the vampires involved having no respect for ghouls and preferring to acquire a subordinate vampire instead (Possibly even as an experiment in finding out whether a white man could support the \u2018gift\u2019 of their bloodline) or just a product of their desire for extreme secrecy - preferring to deal with other vampires almost solely through a proxy and therefore making sure those vampires would display at least the smallest amount of respect with \u2018The Family\u2019 being required to exert themselves to demonstrate why their ghouls are to be respected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T10:57:55-07:00","id":1551974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551947#post1551947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can\u2019t speak for the rest, but I know enough about classical history to confirm that \u2018hortator\u2019 is the term for a war-galley\u2019s equivalent to the coxswain in a modern competitive rowing team (Though my understanding is that the war galleys of the classical world were more often manned by paid professionals, not slave labour).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good to know that is actually the case. I did not know the term before and had to google it. While I did read it was the title of the galley drummer, the only source for it I could find was Ben-Hur which is not exactly a primary source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551947#post1551947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m assuming that the \u2018Hortator\u2019 in question had some history at sea (Or at least of \u2018encouraging\u2019 a captive audience) to help explain the name; I also wonder if this might have been an individual who made common cause with the Spanish at some point (Possibly one of the peoples subject to the Aztecs who sided with the Spanish to oust their former lords and masters, only to acquire a new set).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aztecs weren't exactly a naval power, and I don't think any Indians had naval technology equivalent to the Greek trireme. Usually the technological comparison made is to Neolithic Sumeria which is some 3000 years behind the Ancient Greeks. Tenochtitlan was build on an island in Lake Texcoco, but as a high priest and counselor to Montezuma, he wouldn't be doing any gruntwork like making sure some local rowboat was being rowed efficiently. I don't think his name derives because of any naval/marine linkage.<br /> <br /> Hortator was definitely one of the Aztecs, not one of their subject peoples. He was counselor to Montezuma after all, supposedly the one who convinced him to welcome Cortes to the city. He supposedly had visions of the future and seems to like staying in the role of counselor to the ruler (as he is to Vannevar like he was to Montezuma). It's possible he was named this by his childe Delfonso if Hortator kept trying to influence/counsel him to take certain actions. If so, that nickname stuck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551947#post1551947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, as for Sullivan being taken into the family as a fledgling rather than a ghoul, this might well be a product of the vampires involved having no respect for ghouls and preferring to acquire a subordinate vampire instead (Possibly even as an experiment in finding out whether a white man could support the \u2018gift\u2019 of their bloodline) or just a product of their desire for extreme secrecy - preferring to deal with other vampires almost solely through a proxy and therefore making sure those vampires would display at least the smallest amount of respect with \u2018The Family\u2019 being required to exert themselves to demonstrate why their ghouls are to be respected.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's possible, but I wonder how much more respectable would be a newly made fledgling childe with no information about vampire society in San Francisco would be than a ghoul when they first arrived. Now once they are established and accepted in the city, I could see them wanting a vampire proxy who could deal with other vampires as an equal. However, it would make more sense to evaluate candidates first to make sure such a future member of the family had the qualities they needed rather than relying on some person whose sole qualification is that he just happened to land on their ship off San Francisco Bay.<br /> <br /> It's possible to combine these points and say Sullivan was originally a ghoul, and by the time the Family decided they needed a proxy to deal with outsiders, they did decide Sullivan was best because of his qualities and level of service as a ghoul. I don't think that's the actual case in the book though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T04:01:07-07:00","id":1551992,"title":"","content":"These are sensible points, but one wonders if Sullivan was chosen for occult, rather than purely rational reasons - perhaps grounded in religion or prophecy (\u201cEmbrace the first soul you meet and you shall know success in the new land\u201d) rather than straightforward policy?<br /> <br /> After all, if any setting is likely to produce political thinking with realpolitik and superstition as intricately tangled-up as Ancient Rome, it\u2019s the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Hortator, I was thinking in terms of his post-Aztec career when wondering if he had some sort of maritime service (and if memory serves, at least some of the operations against Tenochtitlan had a waterborne component on Lake so there\u2019s room for the Aztecs to employ boats, whether for escape or some other manoeuvre: heck, the name might just stem from \u2018Hortator\u2019 having been sighted in the rear of a boat shouting at the towers to get a move on or he\u2019d kill them before the white man did).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T10:58:05-07:00","id":1552004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551992#post1551992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are sensible points, but one wonders if Sullivan was chosen for occult, rather than purely rational reasons - perhaps grounded in religion or prophecy (\u201cEmbrace the first soul you meet and you shall know success in the new land\u201d) rather than straightforward policy?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's possible. In the book there's evidence that the Family moved to San Francisco on behalf of some entity back in China, and the Grandfather is doing its bidding. (What that entity is, is not revealed. It could be a vampire, spirit, demon, or something else.) However, in this particular case, the evidence is against it. Sullivan was not the only crimp to approach the boat, and the Family killed the others leaving only him. And later there is a section where Sullivan reveals the Family intended to dispose of him (i.e. destroy him) after he served his initial purpose, but his sire (Kwon) argued against it because by that point they were lovers.<br /> <br /> There's several weaknesses in the book, and why Sullivan was embraced instead of being made a ghoul was one of them. It's a common issue with many character creations to be honest. A lot of character backstories (both PC and NPC) tend to be along the lines of &quot;I'm embraced because I'm useful&quot;, but there's nothing written about why this person would be more useful as a vampire (which requires a lot more investment in time and energy) than a ghoul, mortal pawn, dominated/blood bound minion, etc. The other big weakness is that the book is written in a way that makes more sense if Sullivan was a neonate when in reality he's an ancillae not that far from elder status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club?p=1551992#post1551992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Hortator, I was thinking in terms of his post-Aztec career when wondering if he had some sort of maritime service (and if memory serves, at least some of the operations against Tenochtitlan had a waterborne component on Lake so there\u2019s room for the Aztecs to employ boats, whether for escape or some other manoeuvre: heck, the name might just stem from \u2018Hortator\u2019 having been sighted in the rear of a boat shouting at the towers to get a move on or he\u2019d kill them before the white man did).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again it's possible because we know very little about Hortator's history. He gets name dropped several times, but doesn't have much screen time. If we assume he followed Delfonso to San Francisco from Mexico (which makes the most sense to me), he's usually in the American southwest desert. Not much opportunity for boats there. There's nothing mentioned about any involvement with boats. Instead, what little we know repeats that this is a spiritual leader, political advisor, and he acts on the visions he receives. So I think it's unlikely we are supposed to imagine naval involvement has any relevance to the name Hortator Simply seeing someone at the end of some boat is unlikely to lead to a nickname that survives five centuries and ends up becoming the name he's known by. However, STs wanting to use the character can certainly fill in any details they wanted and use him differently than I will.<br /> <br /> I should also mention that this guy is not someone who wanted to fight the Spanish. His visions convinced him any resistance would be futile, and he was a willing collaborator. He would have been one of the guys who quickly adjusted to the Spanish arrival. The details of his life during the period of the Conquest is not known. So it's not clear who embraced him or why, but he had to embrace Delfonso fairly shortly thereafter since Delfonso too was a mortal during the Conquest. (Again I'll note I read the books rather fast and could very well have glossed over something significant. If others have actual details, feel free to post them.)<br /> <br /> The author Keith Herber clearly had some setting background in mind where Hortator had much more importance than what gets revealed in these books. As a one off character, he'd be easy to ignore except that there are at least two others of this line of mysterious &quot;Aztec vampires&quot; of unknown clan. It would have been interesting to see a San Francisco By Night sourcebook from him as he was veteran in the RPG industry with Chaosium before working with White Wolf. Since Chaosium was based in the Bay Area, I assume Keith lived there at some point and knew the local area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T12:01:52-07:00","id":1552006,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019d like to point out that Plato, grandfather of Western Philosophy, is said to have been born Aristocles and been nicknamed \u2018Plato\u2019 because he was an Absolute Unit (\u2018Plato\u2019 meaning \u2018Broad, thick\u2019).<br /> <br /> Heck, whole nations and generations have equated the word \u2018Caesar\u2019 with Imperial Majesty, despite \u2018Caesar\u2019 almost certainly deriving from a family nickname being \u2018Hairy\u2019.<br /> <br /> Trust me, if there\u2019s one thing History and Mythology has a long record of, it\u2019s quite distinguished individuals being condemned to be forever remembered by nicknames.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T12:03:56-07:00","id":1552007,"title":"","content":"Oh and I quite agree that one would have loved to see a SAN FRANCISCO BY NIGHT sourcebook by the author of PRINCE OF THE CITY (Though possibly not by that title - it lacks a certain Gothic flourish - BLOOD ON THE GOLDEN GATE, perhaps?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}